    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is a non-decreasing function of the number of documents retrieved? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. precision\nB. recall\nC. accuracy\nD. mean average precision\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Recall is defined as the ratio of the number of relevant documents retrieved to the total number of relevant documents, so as more documents are retrieved (including relevant ones), recall either increases or stays the same—it never decreases. Precision, on the other hand, can decrease with more documents if they are irrelevant, and accuracy and mean average precision are not necessarily monotonic with respect to the number of retrieved documents. Therefore, recall is the only non-decreasing function among the options.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
