    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency) weight is low when a term appears in almost all documents because the inverse document frequency (IDF) component decreases significantly. Since IDF is calculated as log(total documents / documents containing the term), if the term is in virtually all documents, IDF approaches zero. Thus, the TF-IDF weight will be lowest.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
