    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef doesValidArrayExist(derived):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines whether there exists a valid binary array original that could have formed derived.\n    \n    The key insight is that for a valid original array to exist, the XOR of all elements in derived must be 0.\n    This is because:\n    - derived[0] = original[0] ⊕ original[1]\n    - derived[1] = original[1] ⊕ original[2]\n    - ...\n    - derived[n-1] = original[n-1] ⊕ original[0]\n    \n    When we XOR all derived elements together, each original[i] appears exactly twice,\n    so they all cancel out (x ⊕ x = 0), leaving us with 0.\n    If the XOR of all derived elements is not 0, no valid original array exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    xor_sum = 0\n    for val in derived:\n        xor_sum ^= val\n    \n    return xor_sum == 0\n```",
