      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nfrom itertools import combinations_with_replacement\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    idx = 0\n    N = int(data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    M = int(data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    \n    wheels = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        C = int(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        P = int(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        S = list(map(int, data[idx:idx+P]))\n        idx += P\n        wheels.append((C, P, S))\n    \n    # Expected values and cost per point for each wheel\n    expected_values = []\n    for C, P, S in wheels:\n        exp_val = sum(S) / P\n        expected_values.append(exp_val)\n    \n    # DP over remaining points needed: dp[r] = minimum expected cost to get at least r points\n    # We only care about r from 0 to M\n    # Use DP with state: dp[r] = minimum expected cost from current state where r is the remaining points needed\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (M + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0.0  # If 0 points are needed, cost is 0\n    \n    # We will iteratively update dp until convergence\n    # Since the state space is small (M <= 100), we can do value iteration\n    converged = False\n    while not converged:\n        new_dp = dp[:]\n        converged = True\n        \n        for r in range(1, M + 1):\n            best_cost = float('inf')\n            for i, (C, P, S) in enumerate(wheels):\n                # Try playing wheel i\n                exp_cost = C\n                # After playing, we get some points and reduce remaining requirement\n                future_cost = 0.0\n                for s in S:\n                    new_r = max(0, r - s)\n                    future_cost += dp[new_r] / P\n                total_exp_cost = exp_cost + future _cost\n                if total_exp_cost < best_cost:\n                    best_cost = total_exp_cost\n            if abs(best_cost - new_dp[r]) > 1e-9:\n                converged = False\n            new_dp[r] = best_cost\n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    print(dp[M])\n\nsolve()\n```",
