      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numRightTriangles(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return 0\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Count number of 1s in each row and column\n    rowCount = [0] * rows\n    colCount = [0] * cols\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                rowCount[i] += 1\n                colCount[j] += 1\n    \n    result = 0\n    \n    # For each cell with value 1, count how many right triangles can be formed\n    # with this cell as the right angle vertex\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                # The cell (i,j) can be the right angle vertex\n                # Number of ways to choose one 1 from the same row (excluding self)\n                # and one 1 from the same column (excluding self)\n                rowOnes = rowCount[i] - 1\n                colOnes = colCount[j] - 1\n                \n                # Each pair forms a right triangle with (i,j) as the right angle\n                result += rowOnes * colOnes\n    \n    return result\n```",
