    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    S = data[1].strip()\n    \n    # Convert string to list of integers\n    A = [int(c) for c in S]\n    \n    # NAND operation\n    def nand(x, y):\n        return 1 if not (x and y) else 0\n    \n    total_sum = 0\n    \n    # We'll compute f(i, j) for all 1 <= i <= j <= N\n    # Instead of recomputing from scratch, we can simulate the chain for each starting index i\n    for i in range(N):\n        current = A[i]\n        total_sum += current\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            current = nand(current, A[j])\n            total_sum += current\n    \n    print(total_sum)\n\nsolve()\n```",
