      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to:\n\n1. Find all special substrings (substrings made of a single character)\n2. Count how many times each special substring occurs\n3. Find the longest length where a special substring of that length occurs at least 3 times\n\nLet me trace through the examples:\n- \"aaaa\": special substrings include \"a\" (4 times), \"aa\" (3 times), \"aaa\" (2 times), \"aaaa\" (1 time). \"aa\" occurs 3 times, so answer is 2.\n- \"abcdef\": no character appears 3+ times, so no special substring can occur 3 times.\n- \"abcaba\": \"a\" appears 3 times, \"b\" appears 2 times, so only \"a\" (length 1) occurs 3+ times.\n\nMy approach:\n1. For each character, find all consecutive runs\n2. For each run of length n, it contributes to the count of special substrings of length 1, 2, ..., n\n3. Specifically, a run of length n contributes (n-i+1) occurrences of special substring of length i\n4. Count all occurrences of each length for each character\n5. Find the maximum length that occurs at least 3 times\n\n```python\ndef longestSpecialSubstring(s):\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    # Count occurrences of special substrings by length\n    length_count = defaultdict(int)\n    \n    i = 0\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    while i < n:\n        # Find the length of current consecutive run\n        char = s[i]\n        j = i\n        while j < n and s[j] == char:\n            j += 1\n        run_length = j - i\n        \n        # For a run of length L, it contains (L - k + 1) substrings of length k\n        for length in range(1, run_length + 1):\n            count_from_this_run = run_length - length + 1\n            length_count[length] += count_from_this_run\n        \n        i = j\n    \n    # Find the maximum length that occurs at least 3 times\n    max_length = -1\n    for length, count in length_count.items():\n        if count >= 3:\n            max_length = max(max_length, length)\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
