      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countSymmetricIntegers(low: int, high: int) -> int:\n    count = 0\n    for num in range(low, high + 1):\n        num_str = str(num)\n        n = len(num_str)\n        # Skip numbers with odd number of digits\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            continue\n        # Split into two halves\n        mid = n // 2\n        first_half = num_str[:mid]\n        second_half = num_str[mid:]\n        # Calculate sum of digits in each half\n        first_sum = sum(int(digit) for digit in first_half)\n        second_sum = sum(int(digit) for digit in second_half)\n        # Check if sums are equal\n        if first_sum == second_sum:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```",
