umber (N*N), so the other cells have numbers 1 to N*N-1.\n    # So if we leave center as the last number and then set it to 'T', then the rest are already 1 to N*N-1.\n    # But we need to renumber: the large number at center is not used for dragon part.\n    # Actually, the dragon parts are 1 to N^2-1, so we don't use the number N^2 at all.\n    \n    # Therefore, we can generate the spiral with numbers 1 to N^2, then at center, remove the value (N^2) and set to 'T',\n    # and that's exactly what we want: the rest of the cells have numbers 1 to N^2-1.\n    # And they are arranged in a continuous path (the spiral path).\n    \n    # But in our spiral generation above, the numbers are assigned in increasing order along the path.\n    # So the path 1-2-3-...-N^2 is exactly the spiral path, which is contiguous by edges.\n    # So removing N^2 (which is at center) and labeling it 'T' gives us the valid arrangement.\n    \n    # Create matrix with spiral fill\n    matrix = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    top, bottom = 0, N-1\n    left, right = 0, N-1\n    num = 1\n    \n    while top <= bottom and left <= right:\n        # left to right on top row\n        for j in range(left, right+1):\n            matrix[top][j] = num\n            num += 1\n        top += 1\n        \n        # top to bottom on right column\n        for i in range(top, bottom+1):\n            matrix[i][right] = num\n            num += 1\n        right -= 1\n        \n        # right to left on bottom row\n        if top <= bottom:\n            for j in range(right, left-1, -1):\n                matrix[bottom][j] = num\n                num += 1\n            bottom -= 1\n        \n        # bottom to top on left column\n        if left <= right:\n            for i in range(bottom, top-1, -1):\n                matrix[i][left] = num\n                num += 1\n            left += 1\n    \n    # Now place Takahashi at center and output\n    cx, cy = N//2, N//2\n    # The current value at center will be N*N