      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    \n    # Parse first line: N and T'\n    first_line = input[0].split()\n    N = int(first_line[0])\n    T_prime = first_line[1]\n    \n    # Read the N strings S_1 to S_N\n    S_list = input[1:1+N]\n    \n    valid_indices = []\n    \n    for idx, S in enumerate(S_list):\n        S = S.strip()\n        len_S = len(S)\n        len_T_prime = len(T_prime)\n        \n        # Check based on the four possible operations\n        \n        # Case 1: T' == T  => S == T'\n        if S == T_prime:\n            valid_indices.append(idx + 1)\n            continue\n            \n        # Case 2: T' is obtained by inserting one char into T\n        # So T is S, and T' should be S with one char inserted => len(T') = len(S) + 1\n        if len_T_prime == len_S + 1:\n            # Check if we can delete one char from T' to get S\n            i = 0\n            j = 0\n            diff = 0\n            while i < len_T_prime and j < len_S:\n                if T_prime[i] != S[j]:\n                    diff += 1\n                    if diff > 1:\n                        break\n                    i += 1  # skip this char in T' (as the inserted one)\n                else:\n                    i += 1\n                    j += 1\n            else:\n                # If we reached the end, check if diff is exactly 1 or if j reached end and i has one extra\n                if diff == 0 and i == len_T_prime and j == len_S:  # extra char at end\n                    valid_indices.append(idx + 1)\n                    continue\n                if diff == 1 and i == len_T_prime and j == len_S:\n                    valid_indices.append(idx + 1)\n                    continue\n            # If we exited early, skip\n            \n        # Case 3: T' is obtained by deleting one char from T\n        # So T is S, and T' is S with one char deleted => len(T') = len(S) - 1\n        elif len_T_prime == len_S - 1:\n            # Check if we can delete one char from S to get T'\n            i = 0\n            j = 0\n            diff = 0\n            while i < len_T_prime and j < len_S:\n                if T_prime[i] != S[j]:\n                    diff += 1\n                    if diff > 1:\n                        break\n                    j += 1  # skip this char in S (the deleted one)\n                else:\n                    i += 1\n                    j += 1\n            else:\n                if diff == 0 and i == len_T_prime and j == len_S:  # deleted at end\n                    valid_indices.append(idx + 1)\n                    continue\n                if diff == 1 and i == len_T_prime and j == len_S:\n                    valid_indices.append(idx + 1)\n                    continue\n        \n        # Case 4: T' is obtained by changing one char in T\n        # So T is S, and T' differs in exactly one char, same length\n        elif len_T_prime == len_S:\n            diff_count = sum(1 for a, b in zip(S, T_prime) if a != b)\n            if diff_count == 1:\n                valid_indices.append(idx + 1)\n    \n    # Output\n    K = len(valid_indices)\n    print(K)\n    if K > 0:\n        print(' '.join(map(str, valid_indices)))\n\nsolve()\n```",
