      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    A = [0] + list(map(int, data[1:1+n]))  # 1-indexed: A[i] is the destination of edge from vertex i\n    \n    # We'll use cycle detection by tracking visited nodes\n    visited = [0] * (n + 1)  # 0: unvisited, 1: visiting, 2: finished\n    \n    def find_cycle(start):\n        path = []\n        current = start\n        \n        # Follow the path until we revisit a node\n        while visited[current] == 0:\n            visited[current] = 1  # mark as visiting\n            path.append(current)\n            current = A[current]\n        \n        # If we've come back to a node currently being visited, we found a cycle\n        if visited[current] == 1:\n            # Find the position of current in path\n            if current in path:\n                pos = path.index(current)\n                cycle = path[pos:]\n                return cycle\n        \n        return None\n    \n    # Try starting from each unvisited node\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if visited[i] == 0:\n            cycle = find_cycle(i)\n            if cycle:\n                print(len(cycle))\n                print(' '.join(map(str, cycle)))\n                return\n\nsolve()\n```",
