      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countPairs(coordinates, k):\n    count = 0\n    point_count = {}\n    \n    for x, y in coordinates:\n        # For each possible XOR value a from 0 to k\n        for a in range(k + 1):\n            b = k - a  # Since a + b = k\n            # We need x1 ^ x2 = a and y1 ^ y2 = b\n            # So x2 = x1 ^ a and y2 = y1 ^ b\n            target_x = x ^ a\n            target_y = y ^ b\n            target_point = (target_x, target_y)\n            \n            if target_point in point_count:\n                count += point_count[target_point]\n        \n        # Add current point to the count\n        current_point = (x, y)\n        point_count[current_point] = point_count.get(current_point, 0) + 1\n    \n    return count\n```",
