      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef kthSmallestAmount(coins, k):\n    def count_multiples(x):\n        \"\"\"Count how many amounts <= x can be made with the given coins\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        n = len(coins)\n        \n        # Use inclusion-exclusion principle\n        # Iterate through all possible subsets of coins\n        for mask in range(1, 1 << n):\n            lcm_val = 1\n            bit_count = 0\n            \n            for i in range(n):\n                if mask & (1 << i):\n                    # Calculate LCM of selected coins in this subset\n                    import math\n                    lcm_val = lcm_val * coins[i] // math.gcd(lcm_val, coins[i])\n                    bit_count += 1\n                    \n                    # Early termination if LCM exceeds x\n                    if lcm_val > x:\n                        break\n            \n            if lcm_val <= x:\n                # Apply inclusion-exclusion: add for odd number of elements, subtract for even\n                if bit_count % 2 == 1:\n                    count += x // lcm_val\n                else:\n                    count -= x // lcm_val\n        \n        return count\n    \n    # Binary search for the kth smallest amount\n    left, right = 1, k * min(coins)\n    \n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if count_multiples(mid) < k:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid\n    \n    return left\n```",
