    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    lines = []\n    for line in sys.stdin:\n        lines.append(line.strip())\n    \n    n = int(lines[0])\n    points = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        x, y = map(int, lines[i].split())\n        points.append((x, y))\n    \n    # For each point, find the farthest point\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_distance = -1\n        farthest_point_id = -1\n        \n        for j in range(n):\n            if i == j:\n                continue\n                \n            # Calculate Euclidean distance\n            x1, y1 = points[i]\n            x2, y2 = points[j]\n            distance = math.sqrt((x1 - x2) ** 2 + (y1 - y2) ** 2)\n            \n            # Update farthest point if this distance is greater,\n            # or if distance is equal but j+1 (ID) is smaller\n            if distance > max_distance or (distance == max_distance and j + 1 < farthest_point_id):\n                max_distance = distance\n                farthest_point_id = j + 1\n                \n        print(farthest_point_id)\n\nsolve()\n```",
