      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef canMakeZero(nums, k):\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # We'll use a difference array to track operations efficiently\n    diff = [0] * (n + 1)\n    operations = 0\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        # Propagate the effect of previous operations\n        operations += diff[i]\n        \n        # Current value after all operations\n        current_val = nums[i] - operations\n        \n        # If current value is negative, we've over-decreased\n        if current_val < 0:\n            return False\n            \n        # If current value is positive, we need to apply operations\n        if current_val > 0:\n            # Check if we can apply an operation starting at this position\n            if i + k > n:\n                return False\n                \n            # Apply 'current_val' operations on subarray starting at i\n            operations += current_val\n            diff[i + k] -= current_val\n    \n    # Check if all elements are exactly 0\n    return operations + diff[n] == 0\n```",
