      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findPermutationDifference(s, t):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the permutation difference between two strings s and t.\n    \n    The permutation difference is the sum of absolute differences between \n    the indices of each character in s and its index in t.\n    \n    Args:\n        s (str): First string with unique characters\n        t (str): Second string, a permutation of s\n    \n    Returns:\n        int: The permutation difference\n    \"\"\"\n    total_difference = 0\n    \n    # For each character in s, find its position in both strings\n    for char in s:\n        index_in_s = s.index(char)\n        index_in_t = t.index(char)\n        total_difference += abs(index_in_s - index_in_t)\n    \n    return total_difference\n```",
