    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_340",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nThere is a grid with 10^9 by 10^9 squares. Let (i, j) denote the square at the (i + 1)-th row from the top and the (j + 1)-th column from the left (0 \\leq i, j \\lt 10^9). (Note the unusual index assignment.)\r\nEach square is black or white. The color of the square (i, j) is represented by a character P[i \\bmod N][j \\bmod N], where B means black, and W means white. Here, a \\bmod b denotes the remainder when a is divided by b.\nAnswer Q queries.\r\nEach query gives you four integers A, B, C, D and asks you to find the number of black squares contained in the rectangular area with (A, B) as the top-left corner and (C, D) as the bottom-right corner.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format. Here, \\text{{query}}_i is the i-th query to be processed.\nN Q\r\nP[0][0]P[0][1]\\dots P[0][N-1]\r\nP[1][0]P[1][1]\\dots P[1][N-1]\r\n\\vdots\r\nP[N-1][0]P[N-1][1]\\dots P[N-1][N-1]\r\n\\text{{query}}_1\r\n\\text{{query}}_2\r\n\\vdots\r\n\\text{{query}}_Q\r\n\nEach query is given in the following format:\nA B C D\n\nOutput\n\nFollow the instructions in the problem statement and print the answers to the queries, separated by newlines.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 1000\n- P[i][j] is W or B.\n- 1 \\leq Q \\leq 2 \\times 10^5\n- 0 \\leq A \\leq C \\lt 10^9\n- 0 \\leq B \\leq D \\lt 10^9\n- N, Q, A, B, C, D are all integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3 2\r\nWWB\r\nBBW\r\nWBW\r\n1 2 3 4\r\n0 3 4 5\n\nSample Output 1\n\n4\r\n7\r\n\nThe figure below illustrates the upper left part of the grid.\n\nFor the first query, the rectangular area with (1, 2) as the top-left corner and (3, 4) as the bottom-right corner, surrounded by the red frame in the figure, contains four black squares.\r\nFor the second query, the rectangular area with (0, 3) as the top-left corner and (4, 5) as the bottom-right corner, surrounded by the blue frame in the figure, contains seven black squares.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n10 5\r\nBBBWWWBBBW\r\nWWWWWBBBWB\r\nBBBWBBWBBB\r\nBBBWWBWWWW\r\nWWWWBWBWBW\r\nWBBWBWBBBB\r\nWWBBBWWBWB\r\nWBWBWWBBBB\r\nWBWBWBBWWW\r\nWWWBWWBWWB\r\n5 21 21 93\r\n35 35 70 43\r\n55 72 61 84\r\n36 33 46 95\r\n0 0 999999999 999999999\n\nSample Output 2\n\n621\r\n167\r\n44\r\n344\r\n500000000000000000",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().splitlines()\n    \n    # Read N and Q\n    N, Q = map(int, data[0].split())\n    \n    # Read the N x N pattern\n    P = []\n    for i in range(1, 1 + N):\n        P.append(data[i].strip())\n    \n    # Precompute the number of black cells in one N x N block\n    total_black = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(N):\n            if P[i][j] == 'B':\n                total_black += 1\n    \n    # Precompute prefix sums for rows and full grid\n    # prefix[i][j] = number of black cells in P[0:i, 0:j]\n    prefix = [[0] * (N + 1) for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        for j in range(1, N + 1):\n            prefix[i][j] = prefix[i-1][j] + prefix[i][j-1] - prefix[i-1][j-1] + (1 if P[i-1][j-1] == 'B' else 0)\n    \n    def count_black_in_block(r1, c1, r2, c2):\n        \"\"\"Count black cells in the block from (r1, c1) to (r2, c2) inclusive\"\"\"\n        if r1 > r2 or c1 > c2:\n            return 0\n        # Normalize to within [0, N)\n        cnt = 0\n        for i in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n            for j in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                if P[i % N][j % N] == 'B':\n                    cnt += 1\n        return cnt\n    \n    def count_black_in_rectangle(a, b, c, d):\n        \"\"\"Count black cells in rectangle (a,b) to (c,d) inclusive\"\"\"\n        # Break rectangle into parts:\n        # Full blocks and partial edges\n        \n        # Total number of complete N x N blocks\n        start_i, end_i = a, c\n        start_j, end_j = b, d\n        \n        # Find the first and last full block indices\n        first_full_i = (a + N - 1) // N * N if a % N != 0 else a\n        first_full_j = (b + N - 1) // N * N if b % N != 0 else b\n        last_full_i = (c + 1) // N * N - 1 if (c + 1) % N != 0 else c\n        last_full_j = (d + 1) // N * N - 1 if (d + 1) % N != 0 else d\n        \n        total = 0\n        \n        # If valid, add full blocks\n        if first_full_i <= last_full_i and first_full_j <= last_full_j:\n            blocks_i = (last_full_i - first_full_i) // N + 1\n            blocks_j = (last_full_j - first_full_j) // N + 1\n            total += blocks_i * blocks_j * total_black\n        else:\n            first_full_i = last_full_i + 1  # No full blocks in i\n            first_full_j = last_full_j + 1  # No full blocks in j\n        \n        # Add top strip: from (a, b) to (min(c, first_full_i - 1), d)\n        if a <= last_full_i - 1:\n            end_row = min(c, first_full_i - 1)\n            total += count_black_in_block(a, b, end_row, d)\n        \n        # Add bottom strip: from (max(last_full_i + 1, a), b) to (c, d)\n        if last_full_i + 1 <= c:\n            start_row = max(last_full_i + 1, a)\n            if start_row <= c:\n                total += count_black_in_block(start_row, b, c, d)\n        \n        # Add left strip: from (first_full_i, b) to (last_full_i, min(d, first_full_j - 1))\n        if first_full_i <= last_full_i and b <= first_full_j - 1:\n            end_col = min(d, first_full_j - 1)\n            total += count_black_in_block(first_full_i, b, last_full_i, end_col)\n        \n        # Add right strip: from (first_full_i, max(first_full_j, last_full_j + 1)) to (last_full_i, d)\n        if first_full_i <= last_full_i and last_full_j + 1 <= d:\n            start_col = max(first_full_j, last_full_j + 1)\n            if start_col <= d:\n                total += count_black_in_block(first_full_i, start_col, last_full_i, d)\n        \n        # However, the above overcounts the corners and misses the structure.\n        # Let's switch to a cleaner modular arithmetic method.\n        \n        # Instead, use divide and conquer by full blocks\n        total = 0\n        \n        # Function to count black in [r1, r2] x [c1, c2] within one block\n        def count_in_single_block(r1, r2, c1, c2):\n            cnt = 0\n            for i in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                for j in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                    if P[i][j] == 'B':\n                        cnt += 1\n            return cnt\n        \n        # Count full N x N blocks\n        full_blocks_i = (c + 1 - a) // N\n        full_blocks_j = (d + 1 - b) // N\n        \n        # But better to align by mod\n        start_i_mod = a % N\n        start_j_mod = b % N\n        end_i_mod = c % N\n        end_i_block = c // N\n        start_i_block = a // N\n        end_j_mod = d % N\n        start_j_block = b // N\n        end_j_block = d // N\n        \n        # Case: within same block\n        if start_i_block == end_i_block and start_j_block == end_j_block:\n            return count_in_single_block(start_i_mod, end_i_mod, start_j_mod, end_j_mod)\n        \n        # Standard method: break into 4 parts: TL, TR, BL, BR and center\n        # We can compute using inclusion\n        def count_up_to(i, j):\n            # Count black cells in [0, i] x [0, j]\n            if i < 0 or j < 0:\n                return 0\n            full_blocks_i = i // N\n            full_blocks_j = j // N\n            rem_i = i % N\n            rem_j = j % N\n            cnt = full_blocks_i * full_blocks_j * total_black\n            # Add right strip\n            if rem_j >= 0:\n                for r in range(0, rem_i + 1):\n                    for c in range(0, N):\n                        if P[r][c] == 'B':\n                            cnt += full_blocks_j\n                # Add bottom strip\n                for r in range(0, N):\n                    for c in range(0, rem_j + 1):\n                        if P[r][c] == 'B':\n                            cnt += full_blocks_i\n                # Add corner\n                cnt += prefix[rem_i + 1][rem_j + 1]\n            else:\n                # rem_i >= 0\n                for r in range(0, rem_i + 1):\n                    for c in range(0, N):\n                        if P[r][c] == 'B':\n                            cnt += full_blocks_j\n            return cnt\n        \n        # But wait, better standard method:\n        # Count from (0,0) to (c,d) minus the parts\n        # Answer is f(c,d) - f(a-1,d) - f(c,b-1) + f(a-1,b-1)\n        def f(r, c):\n            if r < 0 or c < 0:\n                return 0\n            full_rows = r // N\n            full_cols = c // N\n            rem_row = r % N\n            rem_col = c % N\n            cnt = full_rows * full_cols * total_black\n            # Add right partial strip (full rows, partial columns)\n            for i in range(N):\n                for j in range(rem_col + 1):\n                    if P[i][j] == 'B':\n                        cnt += full_rows\n            # Add bottom partial strip (partial rows, full columns)\n            for i in range(rem_row + 1):\n                for j in range(N):\n                    if P[i][j] == 'B':\n                        cnt += full_cols\n            # Add bottom-right corner\n            for i in range(rem_row + 1):\n                for j in range(rem_col + 1):\n                    if P[i][j] == 'B':\n                        cnt += 1\n            return cnt\n        \n        result = f(c, d) - f(a-1, d) - f(c, b-1) + f(a-1, b-1)\n        return result\n    \n    # Process queries\n    out_lines = []\n    for i in range(1 + N, 1 + N + Q):\n        A, B, C, D = map(int, data[i].split())\n        res = count_black_in_rectangle(A, B, C, D)\n        out_lines.append(str(res))\n    \n    print('\\n'.join(out_lines))\n\nmain()\n```",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
