      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_eaten_cookie():\n    # Read input\n    H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        grid.append(input().strip())\n    \n    # Find all '#' positions\n    cookie_positions = []\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                cookie_positions.append((i, j))\n    \n    # Find the bounding rectangle of all cookies\n    min_row = min(pos[0] for pos in cookie_positions)\n    max_row = max(pos[0] for pos in cookie_positions)\n    min_col = min(pos[1] for pos in cookie_positions)\n    max_col = max(pos[1] for pos in cookie_positions)\n    \n    # The original rectangle should be from (min_row, min_col) to (max_row, max_col)\n    # But one cookie is missing, so we need to find which position in this rectangle has no cookie\n    \n    # Check each position in the expected rectangle\n    for i in range(min_row, max_row + 1):\n        for j in range(min_col, max_col + 1):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                # This is the missing cookie\n                print(i + 1, j + 1)  # Convert to 1-indexed\n                return\n\nfind_eaten_cookie()\n```",
