    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minOperations(nums, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the minimum number of operations needed to make the median of nums equal to k.\n    \n    Args:\n        nums: List of integers\n        k: Target median value\n    \n    Returns:\n        Minimum number of operations needed\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    # Sort the array to find current median\n    nums_sorted = sorted(nums)\n    \n    # Find the current median\n    # If n is odd, median is at index n//2\n    # If n is even, median is the larger of the two middle elements, which is at index n//2\n    median_idx = n // 2\n    current_median = nums_sorted[median_idx]\n    \n    # If current median is already k, no operations needed\n    if current_median == k:\n        return 0\n    \n    operations = 0\n    \n    # To change the median to k, we need to modify elements such that\n    # after sorting, the element at position median_idx becomes k\n    \n    # If k < current_median, we need to decrease some elements\n    # We should decrease elements from the median position and to the right\n    # until the median becomes k\n    if k < current_median:\n        # Count how many elements from median_idx to end need to be decreased to k or below\n        for i in range(median_idx, n):\n            if nums_sorted[i] > k:\n                operations += nums_sorted[i] - k\n    else:  # k > current_median\n        # Count how many elements from start to median_idx need to be increased to k or above\n        for i in range(median_idx + 1):\n            if nums_sorted[i] < k:\n                operations += k - nums_sorted[i]\n    \n    return operations\n```",
