      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to count the number of stable binary arrays with exactly `zero` zeros and `one` ones, where no subarray longer than `limit` contains only identical elements.\n\nThis is a dynamic programming problem. The key insight is that I need to track:\n1. The number of zeros remaining\n2. The number of ones remaining\n3. The current run length of the last element (to ensure we don't exceed the limit)\n\nI'll use DP where `dp[i][j][k][last]` represents the number of ways to place `i` zeros and `j` ones, where the last `k` elements are the same digit `last` (0 or 1).\n\nHowever, I can optimize this by realizing that I only need to track the count of continuous same elements at the end.\n\n```python\ndef numberOfStableArrays(zero: int, one: int, limit: int) -> int:\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # dp[i][j][k][l] = number of ways to arrange i zeros and j ones\n    # where the last k elements are all l (0 or 1)\n    # We can optimize by using dp[i][j][last_count][last_digit]\n    \n    # Use a 3D DP: dp[i][j][last] where last represents the run length of the last digit\n    # But we need to track which digit it is, so we'll use two separate states\n    \n    # dp[i][j][k][d] = number of ways with i zeros, j ones, k consecutive d's at the end\n    # d = 0 or 1\n    \n    # Initialize memoization dictionary\n    memo = {}\n    \n    def dp(zeros_left, ones_left, last_run, last_digit):\n        if zeros_left == 0 and ones_left == 0:\n            return 1\n        \n        if (zeros_left, ones_left, last_run, last_digit) in memo:\n            return memo[(zeros_left, ones_left, last_run, last_digit)]\n        \n        result = 0\n        \n        # Try placing a 0\n        if zeros_left > 0:\n            if last_digit == 0:\n                # Continuing a run of 0s\n                if last_run < limit:\n                    result = (result + dp(zeros_left - 1, ones_left, last_run + 1, 0)) % MOD\n            else:\n                # Starting a new run of 0s\n                result = (result + dp(zeros_left - 1, ones_left, 1, 0)) % MOD\n        \n        # Try placing a 1\n        if ones_left > 0:\n            if last_digit == 1:\n                # Continuing a run of 1s\n                if last_run < limit:\n                    result = (result + dp(ones_left - 1, zeros_left, last_run + 1, 1)) % MOD\n            else:\n                # Starting a new run of 1s\n                result = (result + dp(ones_left - 1, zeros_left, 1, 1)) % MOD\n        \n        memo[(zeros_left, ones_left, last_run, last_digit)] = result\n        return result\n    \n    total = 0\n    # Start with either 0 or 1\n    if zero > 0:\n        total = (total + dp(zero - 1, one, 1, 0)) % MOD\n    if one > 0:\n        total = (total + dp(zero, one - 1, 1, 1)) % MOD\n    \n    return total\n```",
