      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the longest common prefix between any pair of integers where one comes from arr1 and the other from arr2.\n\nMy approach:\n1. For each number in arr1, I'll generate all its prefixes\n2. Store these prefixes in a set for O(1) lookup\n3. For each number in arr2, I'll check all its prefixes from longest to shortest\n4. The first prefix that exists in the set from arr1 will be the longest common prefix for that pair\n5. Keep track of the maximum length found\n\n```python\ndef longestCommonPrefix(arr1, arr2):\n    # Generate all prefixes from arr1\n    prefixes_set = set()\n    \n    for num in arr1:\n        str_num = str(num)\n        # Add all prefixes of this number\n        for i in range(1, len(str_num) + 1):\n            prefixes_set.add(str_num[:i])\n    \n    max_length = 0\n    \n    # Check all prefixes from arr2 numbers\n    for num in arr2:\n        str_num = str(num)\n        # Check prefixes from longest to shortest\n        for i in range(len(str_num), 0, -1):\n            prefix = str_num[:i]\n            if prefix in prefixes_set:\n                max_length = max(max_length, len(prefix))\n                break  # Found the longest prefix for this number\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
