      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumSum(n, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum possible sum of a k-avoiding array of length n.\n    \n    A k-avoiding array has no pair of distinct elements that sum to k.\n    \n    Args:\n        n: Length of the array\n        k: Target sum to avoid\n    \n    Returns:\n        Minimum possible sum of a k-avoiding array of length n\n    \"\"\"\n    # We want to use the smallest possible positive integers\n    # that don't form pairs summing to k\n    \n    used = set()\n    result = 0\n    current = 1\n    \n    while len(used) < n:\n        # Check if current number can be added\n        # It can be added if its complement (k - current) is not already in used\n        complement = k - current\n        if complement not in used:\n            used.add(current)\n            result += current\n        current += 1\n    \n    return result\n```",
