      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    T = input().strip()\n    N = int(input().strip())\n    \n    bags = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        line = input().split()\n        A_i = int(line[0])\n        strings = line[1:A_i+1]\n        bags.append(strings)\n    \n    # dp[i] = minimum cost to make prefix T[0:i] \n    # Initialize with infinity, except dp[0] = 0 (empty string costs 0)\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dp = [INF] * (len(T) + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    # Process each bag\n    for bag in bags:\n        # Create new dp array for this step since we can only use one string per bag\n        new_dp = dp[:]\n        \n        # For each possible current position in T\n        for pos in range(len(T) + 1):\n            if dp[pos] == INF:\n                continue\n                \n            # Try each string in current bag\n            for s in bag:\n                # Check if we can append this string starting from position pos\n                if pos + len(s) <= len(T) and T[pos:pos + len(s)] == s:\n                    new_dp[pos + len(s)] = min(new_dp[pos + len(s)], dp[pos] + 1)\n        \n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    # Answer is the minimum cost to form entire string T\n    result = dp[len(T)] if dp[len(T)] != INF else -1\n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
