      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    \n    # Read edges\n    edges = []\n    index = 1\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        a = int(data[index]); b = int(data[index + 1]); index += 2\n        edges.append((a, b))\n    \n    # Read C values\n    C = list(map(int, data[index:index + n]))\n    \n    # Build adjacency list\n    graph = defaultdict(list)\n    for a, b in edges:\n        graph[a].append(b)\n        graph[b].append(a)\n    \n    # First, pick an arbitrary root (1) and do a DFS to compute:\n    # - subtree sums of C values\n    # - total distance from root to all nodes weighted by C\n    \n    def dfs(u, parent):\n        # Returns (subtree_c_sum, total_dist_from_u)\n        subtree_c_sum = C[u - 1]  # C is 0-indexed, vertices are 1-indexed\n        total_dist = 0\n        \n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if v == parent:\n                continue\n            child_c_sum, child_dist = dfs(v, u)\n            subtree_c_sum += child_c_sum\n            # Each node in subtree of v is one edge further from u\n            total_dist += child_dist + child_c_sum\n        \n        return subtree_c_sum, total_dist\n    \n    # Step 1: Pick vertex 1 as root, compute total f(1)\n    total_c_sum, f_root = dfs(1, -1)\n    \n    # If we move from parent to child, we can compute f(child) from f(parent)\n    # When moving from u to v:\n    # - For all nodes in subtree of v: distance decreases by 1 -> subtract sum of C in subtree of v\n    # - For all other nodes: distance increases by 1 -> add (total_c_sum - sum of C in subtree of v)\n    # So: f(v) = f(u) - subtree_c[v] + (total_c_sum - subtree_c[v]) = f(u) + total_c_sum - 2 * subtree_c[v]\n    \n    # We need to compute subtree sums for all nodes\n    subtree_c = [0] * (n + 1)\n    \n    def compute_subtree_c(u, parent):\n        res = C[u - 1]\n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if v == parent:\n                continue\n            res += compute_subtree_c(v, u)\n        subtree_c[u] = res\n        return res\n    \n    compute_subtree_c(1, -1)\n    \n    # Now do BFS/DFS from root to compute f(v) for all v\n    min_f = f_root\n    stack = [(1, f_root)]\n    \n    while stack:\n        u, f_u = stack.pop()\n        min_f = min(min_f, f_u)\n        \n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if v != u and (u == 1 or v != 1 and f_u + total_c_sum - 2 * subtree_c[v] != f_u):  # avoid revisiting parent\n                # Compute f(v) from f(u)\n                f_v = f_u + total_c_sum - 2 * subtree_c[v]\n                stack.append((v, f_v))\n    \n    # Actually, let's do it more carefully with proper parent tracking\n    min_f = f_root\n    visited = set()\n    stack = [(1, f_root)]\n    visited.add(1)\n    \n    while stack:\n        u, f_u = stack.pop()\n        min_f = min(min_f, f_u)\n        \n        for v in graph[u]:\n            if v not in visited:\n                visited.add(v)\n                f_v = f_u + total_c_sum - 2 * subtree_c[v]\n                stack.append((v, f_v))\n    \n    print(min_f)\n\nsolve()\n```",
