make X match S, then S must be constructible by overlapping instances of T\n    # This means every character in S must be part of at least one valid T placement,\n    # and the placements must be compatible.\n    \n    # Let's use BFS/DFS to see if we can cover the entire string\n    # dp[i] = whether we can fully construct the prefix ending at position i\n    dp = [False] * (N + 1)\n    dp[0] = True  # Empty prefix is constructible\n    \n    for i in range(N):\n        if not dp[i]:\n            continue\n            \n        # From position i, try to place T\n        for j in range(i, min(N - M + 1, i + M)):  # We can jump at most M positions forward\n            if j + M <= N and S[j:j+M] == T:\n                dp[j + M] = True\n    \n    # But this approach has issues. Let's reconsider.\n    \n    # Key insight: Since we can apply the operation any number of times, we can overlap Ts.\n    # The necessary and sufficient condition is that every character in S must be coverable by T,\n    # and the pattern must be consistent.\n    \n    # Actually, let's use a different approach:\n    # We can make X match S if and only if S can be partitioned into overlapping or adjacent segments of T.\n    \n    # But this is complex. Let's use a simpler approach:\n    # Try to simulate the construction greedily from left to right.\n    \n    # Actually, here's a better approach:\n    # We can make X match S if and only if for every position i in S,\n    # either S[i] can be part of some occurrence of T in S.\n    \n    # But this isn't enough. Consider: can we actually construct it?\n    \n    # Let's use dynamic programming where dp[i] = True if we can construct the first i characters\n    dp = [False] * (N + 1)\n    dp[0] = True\n    \n    for i in range(N):\n        if not dp[i]:\n            continue\n            \n        # Try placing T starting at position i\n        if i + M <= N and S[i:i+M] == T:\n            dp[i + M] = True\n    \n    if dp[N]:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
