    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    \n    # Read input\n    H, W = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        grid.append(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    \n    # Target sequence\n    target = \"snuke\"\n    \n    # Directions: 8 possible directions (horizontal, vertical, diagonal)\n    directions = [\n        (-1, 0),  # up\n        (1, 0),   # down\n        (0, -1),  # left\n        (0, 1),   # right\n        (-1, -1), # up-left\n        (-1, 1),  # up-right\n        (1, -1),  # down-left\n        (1, 1)    # down-right\n    ]\n    \n    # Check if a given starting position and direction forms the \"snuke\" sequence\n    def check_sequence(r, c, dr, dc):\n        positions = []\n        for i in range(5):\n            nr, nc = r + i * dr, c + i * dc\n            if nr < 0 or nr >= H or nc < 0 or nc >= W:\n                return None\n            if grid[nr][nc] != target[i]:\n                return None\n            positions.append((nr + 1, nc + 1))  # Convert to 1-indexed\n        return positions\n    \n    # Search for the sequence\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if grid[r][c] == 's':  # Only start from 's'\n                for dr, dc in directions:\n                    result = check_sequence(r, c, dr, dc)\n                    if result is not None:\n                        for pos in result:\n                            print(pos[0], pos[1])\n                        return\n\nsolve()\n```",
