      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    N, M = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    \n    # Build the tree\n    children = defaultdict(list)\n    if N > 1:\n        parents = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split()))\n        for i in range(2, N + 1):\n            parent = parents[i - 2]  # p_2 is at index 0\n            children[parent].append(i)\n    \n    # Read insurance policies\n    insurances = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        x, y = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n        insurances.append((x, y))\n    \n    # Track covered people\n    covered = set()\n    \n    # For each insurance policy\n    for x, y in insurances:\n        # BFS to find all covered people (x and descendants up to y generations)\n        queue = deque([(x, 0)])  # (person, generation)\n        covered.add(x)  # The buyer is always covered\n        \n        while queue:\n            person, gen = queue.popleft()\n            \n            # If we haven't reached the generation limit, add children\n            if gen < y:\n                for child in children[person]:\n                    if child not in covered:\n                        covered.add(child)\n                    queue.append((child, gen + 1))\n    \n    print(len(covered))\n\nsolve()\n```",
