      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum cost to convert `source` to `target` using the given transformation rules. This is a shortest path problem where I need to find the minimum cost to transform each character from source to target.\n\nThe key insights are:\n1. I need to find the shortest path (minimum cost) between any two characters using the given transformations\n2. I can use Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find the minimum cost between all pairs of characters\n3. For each position where source[i] != target[i], I need to add the minimum transformation cost\n4. If any character cannot be transformed to its target, return -1\n\n```python\ndef minimumCost(source, target, original, changed, cost):\n    # Initialize distance matrix with infinity\n    # Using 26x26 matrix for lowercase letters a-z\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dist = [[INF] * 26 for _ in range(26)]\n    \n    # Distance from a character to itself is 0\n    for i in range(26):\n        dist[i][i] = 0\n    \n    # Fill direct edges from the given transformations\n    for i in range(len(original)):\n        orig_char = ord(original[i]) - ord('a')\n        chng_char = ord(changed[i]) - ord('a')\n        # Keep the minimum cost if there are multiple edges\n        dist[orig_char][chng_char] = min(dist[orig_char][chng_char], cost[i])\n    \n    # Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find shortest paths between all pairs\n    for k in range(26):\n        for i in range(26):\n            for j in range(26):\n                if dist[i][k] != INF and dist[k][j] != INF:\n                    dist[i][j] = min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j])\n    \n    # Calculate total cost to convert source to target\n    total_cost = 0\n    n = len(source)\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        if source[i] != target[i]:\n            src_idx = ord(source[i]) - ord('a')\n            tgt_idx = ord(target[i]) - ord('a')\n            \n            # Check if transformation is possible\n            if dist[src_idx][tgt_idx] == INF:\n                return -1\n                \n            total_cost += dist[src_idx][tgt_idx]\n    \n    return total_cost\n```",
