      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to:\n\n1. Find all substrings where each character appears exactly k times\n2. Ensure that adjacent characters have an alphabet difference of at most 2\n3. Count such \"complete\" substrings\n\nKey insights:\n- For a substring to have each character appear exactly k times, if there are `n` distinct characters, the substring length must be `n * k`\n- The constraint on adjacent character difference means we can split the string at positions where consecutive characters differ by more than 2\n- For each valid segment, I can check all possible numbers of distinct characters from 1 to 26\n\nLet me trace through the examples:\n- Example 1: \"igigee\", k=2\n  - 'i'=8, 'g'=6, 'e'=4 in alphabet positions\n  - Differences: |i-g|=|8-6|=2≤2, |g-i|=2≤2, |i-g|=2≤2, |g-e|=2≤2, |e-e|=0≤2\n  - So the whole string is valid for adjacency constraint\n  - Need to find substrings where each char appears exactly 2 times\n\n```python\ndef countCompleteSubstrings(word, k):\n    def is_valid_segment(s, k):\n        \"\"\"Count complete substrings in segment s\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        n = len(s)\n        \n        # Try all possible numbers of distinct characters (1 to 26)\n        for distinct in range(1, 27):\n            substring_len = distinct * k\n            if substring_len > n:\n                break\n                \n            # Use sliding window of length substring_len\n            char_count = {}\n            \n            # Initialize first window\n            for i in range(substring_len):\n                char_count[s[i]] = char_count.get(s[i], 0) + 1\n            \n            # Check if first window is complete\n            if (len(char_count) == distinct and \n                all(cnt == k for cnt in char_count.values())):\n                count += 1\n            \n            # Slide the window\n            for i in range(substring_len, n):\n                # Add new character\n                char_count[s[i]] = char_count.get(s[i], 0) + 1\n                # Remove old character\n                old_char = s[i - substring_len]\n                char_count[old_char] -= 1\n                if char_count[old_char] == 0:\n                    del char_count[old_char]\n                \n                # Check if current window is complete\n                if (len(char_count) == distinct and \n                    all(cnt == k for cnt in char_count.values())):\n                    count += 1\n        \n        return count\n    \n    if not word:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Split word into segments where adjacent characters differ by at most 2\n    segments = []\n    start = 0\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(word) + 1):\n        if i == len(word) or abs(ord(word[i]) - ord(word[i-1])) > 2:\n            if i > start:\n                segments.append(word[start:i])\n            start = i\n    \n    result = 0\n    for segment in segments:\n        result += is_valid_segment(segment, k)\n    \n    return result\n```",
