    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumMoves(nums, k, maxChanges):\n    n = len(nums)\n    ones = [i for i in range(n) if nums[i] == 1]\n    total_ones = len(ones)\n    \n    # If we already have enough ones, we just need to collect them\n    if total_ones >= k:\n        # Try each possible starting position for Alice\n        min_moves = float('inf')\n        \n        for alice_index in range(n):\n            # Count how many ones we can collect initially\n            initial_pickup = 1 if nums[alice_index] == 1 else 0\n            remaining_needed = k - initial_pickup\n            \n            if remaining_needed <= 0:\n                min_moves = min(min_moves, 0)\n                continue\n                \n            # Calculate minimum moves to collect remaining ones\n            # We can bring ones to alice_index by swapping\n            moves = 0\n            collected = 0\n            \n            # Create a list of distances from each 1 to alice_index\n            distances = []\n            for one_pos in ones:\n                if one_pos != alice_index:\n                    distances.append(abs(one_pos - alice_index))\n            \n            distances.sort()\n            \n            # Take the closest remaining_needed ones\n            if len(distances) >= remaining_needed:\n                moves = sum(distances[:remaining_needed])\n                min_moves = min(min_moves, moves)\n                \n        return min_moves\n    \n    # If we don't have enough ones, we need to create some\n    else:\n        needed_ones = k - total_ones\n        # We need to create 'needed_ones' new ones and collect all existing ones\n        # plus the newly created ones\n        \n        min_moves = float('inf')\n        \n        for alice_index in range(n):\n            # Initial pickup\n            initial_pickup = 1 if nums[alice_index] == 1 else 0\n            total_needed = k - initial_pickup\n            \n            if total_needed == 0:\n                min_moves = min(min_moves, 0)\n                continue\n            \n            # We need to both create new ones and move existing ones\n            # First, figure out how many new ones we can create (limited by maxChanges)\n            creatable = min(maxChanges, needed_ones)\n            remaining_after_creation = needed_ones - creatable\n            \n            # If we still need more ones than we can create, impossible case\n            # But per constraint maxChanges + sum(nums) >= k, so this shouldn't happen\n            \n            # Calculate minimum cost\n            moves = 0\n            available_creations = creatable\n            \n            # For creating new ones optimally, we should create them as close to alice_index as possible\n            # and then move existing ones\n            distances = []\n            for one_pos in ones:\n                if one_pos != alice_index:\n                    distances.append(abs(one_pos - one_pos))\n            \n            # We need to account for both moving existing ones and creating new ones\n            # When we create a new one at position j, we need 1 move, then |j - alice_index| moves to bring it\n            # So total cost for a created one at distance d is 1 + d\n            # For existing ones, cost is just the distance\n            \n            # Let's try different strategies\n            strategy_moves = float('inf')\n            \n            # Sort existing one distances\n            existing_distances = sorted([abs(pos - alice_index) for pos in ones if pos != alice_index])\n            \n            # We can use up to 'available_creations' creations\n            # For each possible number of creations to actually use\n            for use_creations in range(min(available_creations, total_needed) + 1):\n                need_from_existing = min(len(existing_distances), total_needed - use_creations)\n                need_from_creation = use_creations\n                \n                if need_from_existing + need_from_creation < total_needed:\n                    continue\n                    \n                # Cost is sum of need_from_existing closest existing ones + need_from_creation * (1 + optimal_placement_cost)\n                # For optimal creation, we'd create at adjacent positions, so minimum additional cost is 1 + 1 = 2\n                # (1 to create, 1 to move to alice_index if created at adjacent position)\n                existing_cost = sum(existing_distances[:need_from_existing]) if need_from_existing > 0 else 0\n                # Minimum cost for creations: create at adjacent cell (cost 1) and move (cost 1)\n                creation_cost = use_creations * 2\n                \n                total_cost = existing_cost + creation_cost\n                strategy_moves = min(strategy_moves, total_cost)\n            \n            min_moves = min(min_moves, strategy_moves)\n        \n        return min_moves\n```",
