      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N, S, M, L = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    # We'll use dynamic programming to find the minimum cost\n    # dp[i] represents the minimum cost to buy at least i eggs\n    # We need to go up to N + 12 (in case we need to overshoot with a 12-pack)\n    max_eggs = N + 12\n    INF = float('inf')\n    \n    # Initialize dp array with infinity\n    dp = [INF] * (max_eggs + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0  # Cost to buy 0 eggs is 0\n    \n    # For each number of eggs from 0 to max_eggs\n    for i in range(max_eggs + 1):\n        if dp[i] == INF:\n            continue\n            \n        # Try buying a pack of 6 eggs\n        if i + 6 <= max_eggs:\n            dp[i + 6] = min(dp[i + 6], dp[i] + S)\n            \n        # Try buying a pack of 8 eggs\n        if i + 8 <= max_eggs:\n            dp[i + 8] = min(dp[i + 8], dp[i] + M)\n            \n        # Try buying a pack of 12 eggs\n        if i + 12 <= max_eggs:\n            dp[i + 12] = min(dp[i + 12], dp[i] + L)\n    \n    # Find the minimum cost for at least N eggs\n    answer = min(dp[N:max_eggs + 1])\n    print(answer)\n\nsolve()\n```",
