      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    \n    # Read input\n    first_line = sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()\n    N = int(first_line[0])\n    X = int(first_line[1])\n    \n    A = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()))\n    \n    # We have N-1 scores so far, need to find the minimum score in the last round\n    # such that the final grade (sum excluding highest and lowest) is at least X\n    \n    min_score = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try all possible scores for the last round (0 to 100)\n    for last_score in range(101):\n        # Create the full list of scores\n        scores = A + [last_score]\n        # Sort to find min and max\n        sorted_scores = sorted(scores)\n        \n        # Calculate final grade: sum excluding the lowest and highest\n        # This means sum from index 1 to N-2 (inclusive) in sorted array\n        final_grade = sum(sorted_scores[1:N-1])\n        \n        # If this gives us the required grade, update minimum\n        if final_grade >= X:\n            min_score = min(min_score, last_score)\n    \n    # If no valid score found, return -1\n    if min_score == float('inf'):\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_score)\n\nsolve()\n```",
