    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to divide an array into 3 contiguous subarrays and minimize the sum of their first elements (costs).\n\nKey insights:\n1. The first element of the entire array must be the first element of the first subarray, so `nums[0]` is always included in the cost.\n2. I need to choose 2 split points to create 3 subarrays.\n3. The cost is the sum of the first element of each subarray.\n4. To minimize the cost, I want the second and third subarrays to start with as small values as possible.\n\nThe first subarray starts at index 0, the second subarray starts at some index i (where 1 ≤ i ≤ n-2), and the third subarray starts at some index j (where i+1 ≤ j ≤ n-1).\n\nSo the total cost would be: `nums[0] + nums[i] + nums[j]`\n\nTo minimize this, I need to find the optimal values of i and j.\n\n```python\ndef minimumCost(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    min_cost = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try all possible split points\n    # First subarray: [0, i-1], second: [i, j-1], third: [j, n-1]\n    # So i ranges from 1 to n-2, j ranges from i+1 to n-1\n    for i in range(1, n-1):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            cost = nums[0] + nums[i] + nums[j]\n            min_cost = min(min_cost, cost)\n    \n    return min_cost\n```",
