    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(nums, freq):\n    \"\"\"\n    Track the frequency of IDs in a collection and return the maximum frequency\n    after each step.\n    \n    Args:\n        nums: List of integers representing IDs\n        freq: List of integers representing frequency changes\n    \n    Returns:\n        List of integers representing the maximum frequency after each step\n    \"\"\"\n    collection = {}  # Dictionary to store ID frequencies\n    ans = []  # Result array\n    \n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        id_val = nums[i]\n        change = freq[i]\n        \n        # Update the frequency of the ID\n        if id_val in collection:\n            collection[id_val] += change\n            # Remove the ID if its frequency becomes 0\n            if collection[id_val] == 0:\n                del collection[id_val]\n        else:\n            # Only add if change is positive (as per constraints)\n            if change > 0:\n                collection[id_val] = change\n        \n        # Find the maximum frequency in the current collection\n        if collection:\n            max_freq = max(collection.values())\n            ans.append(max_freq)\n        else:\n            ans.append(0)\n    \n    return ans\n```",
