      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    N, Q = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    S = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    \n    # Preprocess: create an array that marks positions where consecutive characters are the same\n    # consecutive[i] = 1 if S[i] == S[i+1], 0 otherwise (for i from 0 to N-2)\n    consecutive = [0] * (N - 1)\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n        if S[i] == S[i + 1]:\n            consecutive[i] = 1\n    \n    # Build prefix sum array for consecutive array\n    prefix_sum = [0] * N\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + consecutive[i]\n    \n    # Process queries\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        l, r = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n        # Convert to 0-based indexing\n        l -= 1\n        r -= 1\n        \n        # Count consecutive same characters in range [l, r-1]\n        # We need to count positions p where l <= p <= r-1 and S[p] == S[p+1]\n        if l >= r:  # Range has only one character or is empty\n            print(0)\n        else:\n            # Use prefix sum to get count from index l to r-1 in consecutive array\n            # The consecutive array has indices 0 to N-2, corresponding to positions (0,1), (1,2), etc.\n            count = prefix_sum[r] - prefix_sum[l]\n            print(count)\n\nsolve()\n```",
