    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getSmallestString(s, k):\n    if k == 0:\n        return s\n    \n    result = []\n    remaining_k = k\n    \n    for char in s:\n        # Convert char to its ASCII value (a=0, b=1, ..., z=25)\n        char_val = ord(char) - ord('a')\n        \n        # Calculate distance from 'a' (which is 0)\n        # In cyclic order, distance from char to 'a' is min(char_val, 26 - char_val)\n        dist_to_a = min(char_val, 26 - char_val)\n        \n        if remaining_k >= dist_to_a:\n            # We can change this character to 'a'\n            result.append('a')\n            remaining_k -= dist_to_a\n        else:\n            # We can't make it 'a', so we make it the lexicographically smallest possible\n            # We can move remaining_k steps from the original character\n            # We prefer moving backward in the cycle (towards 'a')\n            if remaining_k <= char_val:\n                # Move backward within the normal alphabet order\n                new_char_val = char_val - remaining_k\n            else:\n                # Move backward past 'a' in the cycle\n                # First move to 'a', then continue from 'z' backward\n                new_char_val = 26 - (remaining_k - char_val)\n            \n            result.append(chr(new_char_val + ord('a')))\n            remaining_k = 0\n    \n    return ''.join(result)\n```",
