    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a 0-indexed integer array nums containing n distinct positive integers. A permutation of nums is called special if:\n\nFor all indexes 0 <= i < n - 1, either nums[i] % nums[i+1] == 0 or nums[i+1] % nums[i] == 0.\n\nReturn the total number of special permutations. As the answer could be large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [2,3,6]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,6,2] and [2,6,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [1,4,3]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,1,4] and [4,1,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= nums.length <= 14\n1 <= nums[i] <= 10^9",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to count special permutations where adjacent elements are divisible by each other (one divides the other evenly).\n\nThis is a dynamic programming problem with bitmasks since:\n1. I need to consider all permutations\n2. The constraint depends on the last element chosen\n3. The array length is up to 14, making bitmask feasible\n\nI'll use DP with state (mask, last_index) where:\n- mask represents which elements have been used\n- last_index is the index of the last element in the current permutation\n\n```python\ndef specialPerm(self, nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Precompute which pairs satisfy the condition\n    valid = [[False] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i != j:\n                valid[i][j] = (nums[i] % nums[j] == 0) or (nums[j] % nums[i] == 0)\n    \n    # dp[mask][last] = number of ways to arrange elements represented by mask\n    # with nums[last] as the last element\n    from functools import lru_cache\n    \n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def dp(mask, last):\n        # Count number of set bits in mask\n        count = bin(mask).count('1')\n        if count == n:\n            return 1\n        \n        result = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            if not (mask & (1 << i)):  # if i-th element not used\n                if count == 0 or valid[last][i]:  # if first element or valid transition\n                    result = (result + dp(mask | (1 << i), i)) % MOD\n        \n        return result\n    \n    return dp(0, 0)\n```",
