      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum number of deletions to make a number divisible by 25.\n\nA number is divisible by 25 if and only if its last two digits form a number that is divisible by 25. The possible endings are: 00, 25, 50, 75.\n\nMy approach:\n1. For each valid ending pattern (00, 25, 50, 75), find the rightmost occurrence of the second digit, then look for the first occurrence of the first digit to the left of it.\n2. Calculate the number of deletions needed to form that pattern.\n3. Return the minimum deletions across all valid patterns.\n4. Also consider the case where we can form \"0\" (all digits deleted except one '0', or just '0').\n\n```python\ndef minimumOperations(num):\n    def countOperations(pattern):\n        last_char, first_char = pattern[1], pattern[0]\n        # Find rightmost occurrence of last_char\n        last_idx = -1\n        for i in range(len(num) - 1, -1, -1):\n            if num[i] == last_char:\n                last_idx = i\n                break\n        \n        if last_idx == -1:\n            return float('inf')\n        \n        # Find rightmost occurrence of first_char to the left of last_idx\n        first_idx = -1\n        for i in range(last_idx - 1, -1, -1):\n            if num[i] == first_char:\n                first_idx = i\n                break\n        \n        if first_idx == -1:\n            return float('inf')\n        \n        # Count deletions: everything after last_idx, everything between first_idx and last_idx except these two, everything before first_idx except we keep digits before first_idx\n        # We keep digits from 0 to first_idx-1, then first_idx, then digits from first_idx+1 to last_idx-1 we may delete some, but actually we want to minimize deletions\n        # Actually, we only need to keep the two digits at first_idx and last_idx, and we can keep any digits before first_idx\n        # Deletions = (len(num) - last_idx - 1) + (last_idx - first_idx - 1) + (deletions needed in prefix, but we don't need to delete prefix)\n        # Actually, we can keep all digits before first_idx, so deletions are:\n        # - All digits after last_idx: len(num) - last_idx - 1\n        # - All digits between first_idx and last_idx except we need to remove everything except potentially keeping some, but we only need the two digits\n        # - We can keep the digits from 0 to first_idx-1, so we don't delete them\n        # - We need to delete digits from first_idx+1 to last_idx-1: that's (last_idx - first_idx - 1) digits\n        # So total deletions = (len(num) - last_idx - 1) + (last_idx - first_idx - 1) = len(num) - first_idx - 2\n        \n        return len(num) - first_idx - 2\n    \n    patterns = [\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"]\n    min_ops = float('inf')\n    \n    for pattern in patterns:\n        ops = countOperations(pattern)\n        min_ops = min(min_ops, ops)\n    \n    # Special case: we can also make the number \"0\" by deleting all digits except one '0'\n    # Or if we delete everything, we get 0\n    # Find any '0' and see how many deletions to keep just that '0'\n    for i in range(len(num)):\n        if num[i] == '0':\n            # Keep this '0', delete everything else\n            min_ops = min(min_ops, len(num) - 1)\n    \n    # If no pattern found and no zeros, we need to delete everything to get 0\n    if min_ops == float('inf'):\n        min_ops = len(num)\n    \n    return min_ops\n```",
