      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from itertools import permutations\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    R = data[1].strip()\n    C = data[2].strip()\n    \n    # We need to assign positions for A, B, C in each row and column\n    # Each row must have exactly one A, one B, one C (in some positions)\n    # Each column must have exactly one A, one B, one C\n    # The leftmost non-empty cell in row i must be R[i]\n    # The topmost non-empty cell in column j must be C[j]\n    \n    # Try all possible placements using backtracking\n    def backtrack(grid, row, col):\n        if row == N:\n            # Check if all columns have exactly one A, B, C\n            for j in range(N):\n                col_chars = [grid[i][j] for i in range(N) if grid[i][j] != '.']\n                if len(col_chars) == 0:\n                    continue\n                if col_chars[0] != C[j]:\n                    return None\n                if sorted(col_chars) != ['A', 'B', 'C']:\n                    return None\n            return [\"\".join(row) for row in grid]\n        \n        if col == N:\n            return backtrack(grid, row + 1, 0)\n        \n        # Skip to next position if we're not at the first non-empty cell in this row\n        # or if we've already placed all three chars in this row\n        row_chars = [grid[row][c] for c in range(col) if grid[row][c] != '.']\n        if len(row_chars) >= 3:\n            return backtrack(grid, row, col + 1)\n        \n        # Try placing '.', 'A', 'B', 'C' at (row, col)\n        # First try leaving it empty\n        grid[row][col] = '.'\n        result = backtrack(grid, row, col + 1)\n        if result is not None:\n            return result\n        \n        # Try placing A, B, C\n        for ch in ['A', 'B', 'C']:\n            # Check if we can place this character\n            has_ch_in_row = ch in [grid[row][c] for c in range(N) if grid[row][c] != '.']\n            has_ch_in_col = ch in [grid[r][col] for r in range(N) if grid[r][col] != '.']\n            if has_ch_in_row or has_ch_in_col:\n                continue\n                \n            # Check leftmost condition for row\n            row_before = [grid[row][c] for c in range(col) if grid[row][c] != '.']\n            if len(row_before) == 0 and ch != R[row]:\n                continue\n                \n            # Check topmost condition for column\n            col_above = [grid[r][col] for r in range(row) if grid[r][col] != '.']\n            if len(col_above) == 0 and ch != C[col]:\n                continue\n                \n            # Place the character\n            grid[row][col] = ch\n            result = backtrack(grid, row, col + 1)\n            if result is not None:\n                return result\n            grid[row][col] = '.'  # backtrack\n            \n        return None\n    \n    # Start with empty grid\n    grid = [['.' for _ in range(N)] for _ in range(N)]\n    result = backtrack(grid, 0, 0)\n    \n    if result is None:\n        print(\"No\")\n    else:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        for row in result:\n            print(row)\n\nsolve()\n```",
