      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countInterestingSubarrays(nums, modulo, k):\n    # Convert the array to 1 if nums[i] % modulo == k, else 0\n    transformed = [1 if num % modulo == k else 0 for num in nums]\n    \n    # Use prefix sum approach with modulo\n    # We want count of subarrays where (prefix[r+1] - prefix[l]) % modulo == k\n    # This is equivalent to (prefix[r+1] - k) % modulo == prefix[l] % modulo\n    \n    prefix_count = [0] * modulo\n    prefix_count[0] = 1  # Empty prefix has sum 0\n    \n    prefix_sum = 0\n    result = 0\n    \n    for val in transformed:\n        prefix_sum = (prefix_sum + val) % modulo\n        # We need to find how many previous prefixes had value (prefix_sum - k) % modulo\n        target = (prefix_sum - k) % modulo\n        result += prefix_count[target]\n        prefix_count[prefix_sum] += 1\n    \n    return result\n```",
