      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    M = int(input())\n    S1 = input().strip()\n    S2 = input().strip()\n    S3 = input().strip()\n    \n    strings = [S1, S2, S3]\n    \n    min_time = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try each digit from 0 to 9\n    for digit in '0123456789':\n        times = []\n        \n        # For each reel, find all possible stopping times that would show this digit\n        for i in range(3):\n            reel_times = []\n            for t in range(M * 3):  # We only need to check up to 3*M since we're looking for minimum\n                if strings[i][t % M] == digit:\n                    reel_times.append(t)\n            if not reel_times:\n                break\n            times.append(reel_times)\n        \n        # If one of the reels can't show this digit, skip\n        if len(times) < 3:\n            continue\n            \n        # Find minimum time to press all three buttons\n        # We need one time from each reel's possible times\n        # The total time is the maximum of the three chosen times\n        min_total_time = float('inf')\n        \n        for t1 in times[0]:\n            for t2 in times[1]:\n                if t2 == t1:  # Can't press two buttons at the same time\n                    continue\n                for t3 in times[2]:\n                    if t3 == t1 or t3 == t2:  # Can't press two buttons at the same time\n                        continue\n                    total_time = max(t1, t2, t3)\n                    min_total_time = min(min_total_time, total, time)\n        \n        if min_total_time != float('inf'):\n            min_time = min(min_time, min_total_time)\n    \n    print(min_time if min_time != float('inf') else -1)\n\nsolve()\n```",
