      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumJumps(nums, target):\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # dp[i] represents the maximum number of jumps to reach index i\n    # Initialize with -infinity to track unreachable states\n    dp = [-float('inf')] * n\n    dp[0] = 0  # We start at index 0, so 0 jumps needed to reach it\n    \n    # Fill the dp array\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(j):\n            # Check if we can jump from index i to index j\n            diff = nums[j] - nums[i]\n            if -target <= diff <= target and dp[i] != -float('inf'):\n                # Update the maximum jumps to reach index j\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[i] + 1)\n    \n    # Return the result\n    return dp[n-1] if dp[n-1] != -float('inf') else -1\n```",
