    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To maximize the entropy $ H(X) $ of a non-negative integer-valued random variable $ X $ with $ \\mathbb{E}[X] = 1 $, the optimal distribution is the geometric distribution with parameter $ p $ such that the mean is 1. For a geometric distribution (starting at 0), $ \\mathbb{E}[X] = \\frac{1-p}{p} = 〆1 \\Rightarrow p = 0.5 $. The entropy of this distribution is $ H(X) = -\\sum_{k=0}^\\infty p(1-p)^k \\log_2(p(1-p)^k) = -\\log_2 p - \\frac{1-p}{p} \\log_2(1-p) $, which evaluates to 2.0 bits.\n\nThus, the maximum entropy is $ \\boxed{B} $.",
