    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9177",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the discrete memoryless channel $Y=XZ$ where $X$ and $Z$ are independent binary random variables that take on values 0 and 1. Let $P(Z=1)=0.5$. Find the capacity of this channel in bits.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.322\nB. 0.500\nC. 0.700\nD. 0.100\nE. 0.750\nF. 1.000\nG. 0.585\nH. 0.322\nI. 0.250\nJ. 0.811\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The channel is defined as $ Y = XZ $, where $ X $ and $ Z $ are independent binary random variables, and $ P(Z=1) = 0.5 $. Since $ Z $ is 0 with probability 0.5 and  1 with probability 0.5, $ Y = 0 $ whenever $ Z = 0 $, regardless of $ X $. This means the channel outputs zero half the time, erasing any input information. This setup corresponds to a binary erasure-like channel with erasure probability 0.5 when $ Z=0 $, but with a multiplicative structure.\n\nThe mutual information $ I(X;Y) $ is maximized when $ X $ is Bernoulli(0.5), and in this case, $ Y $ is 0 with probability 0.5 (when $ Z=0 $) and equal to $ X $ with probability 0.5 (when $ Z=1 $). Then $ H(Y|X) = 0 $, and $ H(Y) $ is the entropy of a binary variable with $ P(Y=1) = P(X=1)P(Z=1) = 0.5 \\cdot 0.5 = 0.25 $, so $ P(Y=1)=0.25 $, $ P(Y=0)=0.75 $. Then $ H(Y) = -0.75\\log_2 0.75 - 0.25\\log_2 0.25 \\approx 0.811 $. Since $ H(Y|X) = 0 $, $ I(X;Y) = H(Y) - H(Y|X) = 0.811 $. Thus, the capacity is approximately 0.811 bits.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
