    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The computation has 40% inherently sequential, so 40 seconds must be done on one processor. The remaining 60 seconds can be parallelized. Using Amdahl's Law, with 2 processors, the speedup is $ \\frac{1}{0.4 + \\frac{0.6}{2}} = \\frac{1}{0.7} \\approx 1.43 $, giving time $ \\frac{100}{1.43} \\approx 70 $ seconds; with 4 processors, $ \\frac{1}{0.4 + \\frac{0.6}{4}} = \\frac{1}{0.55} \\approx 1.82 $, giving about 55 seconds.\n\nThus, the best possible times are approximately 70 and 55 seconds.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
