    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that $(X, Y, Z)$ are jointly Gaussian and that $X \\rightarrow Y \\rightarrow Z$ forms a Markov chain. Let $X$ and $Y$ have correlation coefficient 0.1 and let $Y$ and $Z$ have correlation coefficient 0.9. Find $I(X;Z)$ in bits.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.45\nB. 1.2\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.9\nE. 0.00587\nF. 0.15\nG. 0.6\nH. 0.7\nI. 0.025\nJ. 0.3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
