    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The random variables $ X_0, X_1, X_2, \\ldots $ are i.i.d. with support on $ \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 100\\} $, so each value has probability $ \\frac{1}{100} $ of occurring. The waiting time $ N $ to the next occurrence of $ X_0 $ (i.e., the first $ k \\geq 1 $ such that $ X_k = X_0 $) follows a geometric distribution with success probability $ p = \\frac{1}{100} $. The expected value of a geometric distribution is $ E[N] = \\frac{1}{p} = 100 $.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{H}",
