      "generated_answer": "Hero's formula (also known as Heron's formula) states that the area of a triangle with sides $A$, $B$, and $C$ is $\\sqrt{s(s-A)(s-B)(s-C)}$, where $s = \\frac{A+B+C}{2}$ is the semi-perimeter. Option F correctly defines $S(A,B,C) = 0.5 \\times (A + B + C)$, which is the semi-perimeter, and $AREA(A,B,C,X) = \\sqrt{X(X-A)(X-B)(X-C)}$, with $X$ representing $s$. Thus, it matches Heron's formula exactly.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
