    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9405",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $X$ be uniformly distributed over $\\{{1, 2, \\ldots, m\\}}$. Assume $m=2^n$ . We ask random questions: Is $X\\in S_1$? Is $X\\in S_2$? ... until only one integer remains. All $2^m$ subsets of $\\{{1, 2, \\ldots, m\\}}$ are equally likely. Suppose we ask $n+\\sqrt{{n}}$ random questions. Use Markov's inequality to find the probability of error (one or more wrong objects remaining) when $n$ goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.3\nB. 0.4\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.0\nE. 0.7\nF. 0.2\nG. 0.5\nH. 1.0\nI. 0.8\nJ. 0.6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
