    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The period of a sum of sinusoids is the least common multiple (LCM) of the individual periods. The first term $\\cos(3\\pi t)$ has frequency $3\\pi$, so its period is $T_1 = \\frac{2\\pi}{3\\pi} = \\frac{2}{3}$. The second term $\\cos(5\\pi t - 0.5\\pi)$ has frequency $5\\pi$, so its period is $T_2 = \\frac{2\\pi}{5\\pi} = \\frac{2}{5}$. The fundamental period of the combined signal is the least common multiple of $\\frac{2}{3}$ and $\\frac{2}{5}$, which is $2$, since it's the smallest number such that both $\\frac{2}{3}$ and $\\frac{2}{5}$ divide evenly into it when considering integer multiples.\n\n$\\boxed{H}$",
