    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following pairs of 8-bit, two's-complement numbers will result in overflow when the members of the pairs are added?\n\nOptions: \nA. 11110000, 00001111\nB. 01111111, 10000000\nC. 00000001, 10000000\nD. 10000001, 10101010\nE. 11111111, 00000001\nF. 11111111, 10000001\nG. 00000000, 10000000\nH. 10000001, 00000001\nI. 10101010, 11111111\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Overflow in two's-complement addition occurs when adding two numbers of the same sign results in a number of the opposite sign. Checking each pair, only option D (10000001 and 10101010) are both negative (leading 1), and their sum is negative, so no overflow; however, option B: 01111111 (positive) + 10000000 (negative) cannot overflow since signs differ. The correct overflow case is **F**: 11111111 (negative) + 10000001 (negative) = negative sum? Actually, sum is 110000000 (9-bit), discarding carry gives 10000000 — still negative — so no overflow? Wait — correct case is **B**: 01111111 + 10000000 = 11111111 (negative result from positive + negative) — no overflow. Rechecking: **A**: 11110000 + 00001111 = 11111111 → negative + positive = negative → no overflow. Correct answer is **B**: 01111111 (max positive) + 10000000 (negative) — different signs — no overflow. Actually, none seem to overflow? Wait — **E**: 11111111 + 00000001 = 00000000 — carry in to sign bit? Overflow = (carry into sign bit) != (carry out). But easiest: overflow only if both same sign and result opposite. **B**: 01111111 (+127), 10000000 (-128) → sum = -1 → -1 sign ≠ + → but inputs different signs → no overflow. Only possible overflow is when both positive and sum negative, or both negative and sum positive. Check **F**: 11111111 (-1) + 10000001 (-127) = -128? Sum: 110000000 → 9 bits → result 10000000 (-128) → correct, still negative → no overflow. **H**: 10000001 (-127) + 00000001 (+1) → -126 → negative + positive = negative → different signs → no overflow. **D**: 10000001 (-127), 10101010 (-86) → sum = -213 → 8-bit min is -128 → must overflow. -127 + (-86) = -213 → which is < -128 → so result wraps → two negatives sum to positive? Compute: 10000001 + 10101010 = 1 00101011 → sum = 00101011 (43) — positive! Both negative, result positive → **overflow**. So **D** overflows.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
