      "generated_answer": "We are given that one chip is chosen at random from 9 total chips: 5 from Company X (1 defective) and 4 from Company Y (2 defective). There are 3 defective chips in total: 1 from X and 2 from Y. Given that the selected chip is defective, we want the probability it came from Company Y. By Bayes' theorem or conditional probability:  \nP(Y | defective) = P(defective and from Y) / P(defective) = (2/9) / (3/9) = 2/3.\n\nThus, the probability is $ \\frac{2}{3} $.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
