      "generated_answer": "We are given the recurrence:\n\n- $ T(1) = 7 $\n- $ T(n+1) = T(n) + 3n $ for $ n \\geq 1 $\n\nUnrolling the recurrence:\n$$\nT(n) = T(1) + 3(1) + 3(2) + \\dots + 3(n-1) = 7 + 3 \\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} k = 7 + 3 \\cdot \\frac{(n-1)n}{2}\n$$\nThis simplifies to:\n$$\nT(n) = 7 + \\frac{3}{2}(n^2 - n) = \\Theta(n^2)\n$$\n\nThus, the order of growth is $ \\Theta(n^2) $.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
