      "generated_answer": "The program reads two integers I and J, then uses a computed GOTO based on the value of (I - J): if I < J, it goes to label 5; if I ≥ J, to label 6. Label 5 prints J, and label 6 prints I — so the smaller value is printed when I < J, and the larger or equal one otherwise. However, since the PRINT statement outputs either I or J depending on which is smaller, it actually prints the **larger** one only when I ≥ J — but this logic is flawed; tracing carefully shows it prints the **larger** in all cases.\n\nWait — correction: IF (I - J) 5,6,6 means: if I - J < 0 → label 5 (print J), if zero or positive → label 6 (print I). So it prints the larger of the two values.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{F}",
