      "generated_answer": "Throughput is determined by the clock cycle time, and since M-7 has a shorter clock cycle (7.5 ns) than M-5 (10 ns), it can complete more instructions per second, making statement I true. However, the latency of a single instruction is the time from start to finish, which for pipelines is (number of stages) × (clock cycle); for M-5 it is 5 × 10 = 50 ns, and for M-7 it is 7 × 7.5 = 52.5 ns, so statement II is false. Statement III is false because although M-7 has higher throughput, actual program execution time depends on many factors including stalls and hazards, so programs do not always run faster on M-7.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
