      "generated_answer": "Aristotle holds that essences (or forms) are not separate, independently existing entities like Plato’s Forms, but are inseparable from the individual things that instantiate them. Therefore, if all members of a species were destroyed, there would be no substrate in which the essence exists, so the essence would cease to exist as well. Thus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{J}",
