    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_25",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use indirect truth tables to determine whether each set of propositions is consistent. If the set is consistent, choose an option with a consistent valuation. (There may be other consistent valuations.)\nD ≡ E\nF ∨ D\n~E · ~F\n\nOptions: \nA. Inconsistent\nB. Consistent. Consistent valuation when D, E, and F are true\nC. Consistent. Consistent valuation when D and E are true and F is false\nD. Consistent. Consistent valuation when D and F are true and E is false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given three propositions:\n\n1. $ D \\equiv E $ (D if and only if E)  \n2. $ F \\lor D $ (F or D)  \n3. $ \\neg E \\cdot \\neg F $ (not E and not F)\n\nFrom (3), $ \\neg E \\cdot \\neg F $, we know $ E = \\text{false} $ and $ F = \\text{false} $.  \nThen from (2), $ F \\lor D $, since $ F $ is false, $ D $ must be true.  \nBut (1) says $ D \\equiv E $, so D and E must have the same truth value. But D is true and E is false — contradiction.\n\nTherefore, the set is inconsistent.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
