      "generated_answer": "The key differences in Islamic finance include the prohibition of interest (riba), avoidance of uncertain (gharar) and speculative (maysir) transactions, and the requirement for financial products to be backed by tangible assets. Options that mention \"profit\" instead of \"interest\" are incorrect, as profit is permissible in Islamic finance when earned through valid contracts. The correct answer is **G**, as it accurately reflects the prohibitions of interest, uncertainty, speculation, and emphasizes tangible asset backing.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
