  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_352",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the date of maturity of a 60-day note dated March 15?\n\nOptions: \nA. May 15\nB. April 15\nC. July 14\nD. April 14\nE. April 13\nF. June 15\nG. June 14\nH. March 16\nI. May 14\nJ. May 13\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the maturity date of a 60-day note dated March 15, count the days:\n\n- March has 31 days, so from March 15 to March 31 is 17 days (including March 15 as day 1 would make it 18, but typically we count from the day after in financial contexts). However, standard practice is to exclude the start date. So from March 16 to March 31 = 16 days.\n- Then we need 44 more days into April: April has 30 days, so 30 days in April brings us to April 30, but 16 (March) + 30 (April) = 46 days. We only need 60 total.\n- Better: From March 15, add 60 days. March 15 + 16 days = end of March (31), so 16 days used, 44 left. April has 30 days → 44 – 30 = 14 days into May: May 14.\n\nThus, the maturity date is May 14.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
