    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, convert the room dimensions to yards: 14'6\" = 14.5 ft = 14.5/3 ≈ 4.83 yd, and 11'3\" = 11.25 ft = 11.25/3 = 3.75 yd. Area = 4.83 × 3.75 ≈ 18.11 sq yd.  \n\nUsing a 15' (5 yd) width, you can cut a piece 5 yd × 3.75 yd = 18.75 sq yd. Cost = 18.75 × $11.95 ≈ $224.06.  \nWith 12' (4 yd) width, you'd need to run it lengthwise (4.83 yd long) but would require seams or extra cutting inefficiency; however, 4 yd × 4.83 yd = 19.32 sq yd > 18.11, but due to practical layout and waste, the 15' width is more efficient and cheaper.  \n\nThus, the 15' width is more economical at $224.06.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
