      "generated_answer": "The open-to-buy (OTB) is calculated as:  \nOTB = (Planned Sales + Planned Markdowns + Planned Ending Inventory) - (Present Inventory + Inventory Commitments)  \nPlugging in the numbers: (6,000 + 500 + 15,000) - (12,000 + 3,000) = 21,500 - 15,000 = $6,500. However, since actual sales ($3,000) and actual markdowns ($200) differ from planned, we adjust planned figures: Revised needed retail = (3,000 + 200 + 15,000) = 18,200; OTB = 18,200 - 15,000 = $3,200. Closest option is **E. $3,300**.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
