from 6:00 p.m. to 2:30 a.m. = 8.5 hours.\n\n540 / 8.5 = 63.5 — not.\n\nOr from 6:00 p.m. to 12:00 a.m. = 6 hours — 90 mph.\n\nNot working.\n\nAlternatively, if the departure is 9:00 a.m., but \"00 p.m.\" — no.\n\nPerhaps \"00 p.m.\" is \"3:00 p.m.\" — typo.\n\n3:00 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. is negative.\n\nUnless next day — 23.5 hours — 540 / 23.5 ≈ 23 — no.\n\nWait — perhaps the context is missing, but the only mathematically clean answer is 540 miles in 3 hours = 180 mph.\n\nAnd 3 hours before 2:30 p.m. is 11:30 a.m.\n\n\"00 p.m.\" might be a typo for \"12:00 p.m.\" or \"11:30 a.m.\"\n\nBut 12:00 p.m. is sometimes written as 12:00, and \"00\" could be a miswrite.\n\nBut departure at 12:00 p.m. and arrival at 2:30 p.m. is 2.5 hours.\n\n540 / 2.5 = 216 — not in options.\n\nBut wait — maybe the travel time is from 6:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. = 3 hours, and arrival is at 9:00 p.m., but the question says 2:30 p.m. — mismatch.\n\nPerhaps the \"2:30 p.m.\" is a typo, and it's 9:00 p.m.\n\nThen from 6:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. = 3 hours.\n\n540 / 3 = 180 mph.\n\nAnd 180 mph is option E.\n\nGiven that 180 is a clean number and others are not, and it's a common type of problem, likely the intended answer is E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
