  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_17",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: George is seen to place an even-money $100,000 bet on the Bulls to win the NBA Finals. If George has a logarithmic utility-of-wealth function and if his current wealth is $1,000,000, what must he believe is the minimum probability that the Bulls will win?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.525\nB. 0.800\nC. 0.450\nD. 0.575\nE. 0.750\nF. 0.350\nG. 0.650\nH. 0.300\nI. 0.700\nJ. 0.400\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this, we use the expected utility framework with a logarithmic utility function $ u(w) = \\ln(w) $. George will take the bet only if the expected utility of betting is at least as great as the utility of not betting. Let $ p $ be his believed probability that the Bulls win. Then:\n\nExpected utility of betting:  \n$ EU = p \\ln(1,000,000 + 100,000) + (1 - p) \\ln(1,000,000 - 100,000) = p \\ln(1,100,000) + (1 - p) \\ln(900,000) $\n\nUtility of not betting:  \n$ \\ln(1,000,000) $\n\nSet $ EU \\geq \\ln(1,000,000) $ and solve for $ p $:\n$ p \\ln(1.1) + (1 - p) \\ln(0.9) \\geq 0 $\n\nThis simplifies to:\n$ p \\geq \\frac{-\\ln(0.9)}{\\ln(1.1) - \\ln(0.9)} \\approx \\frac{0.10536}{0.09531 + 0.10536} \\approx \\frac{0.10536}{0.20067} \\approx 0.525 $\n\nThus, George must believe the probability is at least about 0.525.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 224,
        "output_tokens": 352,
        "total_tokens": 576
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
