  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_438",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investor has utility function $U(x) = x^{{1/4}}$ for salary. He has a new job offer which pays $80,000 with a bonus. The bonus will be $0, $10000, $20000, $30000, $40000, $50000, or $60000, each with equal probability. What is the certainty equivalent value of this job offer?\n\nOptions: \nA. 100000\nB. 108610\nC. 110000\nD. 105000\nE. 90000\nF. 130000\nG. 120000\nH. 85000\nI. 95000\nJ. 115000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The certainty equivalent is the amount $ x $ such that $ U(x) = \\mathbb{E}[U(\\text{total salary})] $. The total salary is $ 80,000 + B $, where $ B $ is the bonus (0 to 60,000 in increments of 10,000, each with probability $ 1/7 $). Compute $ \\mathbb{E}[U(80000 + B)] = \\frac{1}{7} \\sum_{k=0}^{6} (80000 + 10000k)^{1/4} $, then solve $ x^{1/4} = \\mathbb{E}[U] $ to get $ x \\approx 108,610 $.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
