    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_573",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: JamesTaggertwishes to paint the walls of his storage room. The room's dimensions are 14' by 10' by 8(1/2)' . One quart of paint costing $9.80 will cover 36 sq. ft. Labor costs is $5 per quart or fractionthere of. Find his cost for painting the room.\n\nOptions: \nA. $210.70\nB. $143.20\nC. $158.40\nD. $177.60\nE. $220.50\nF. $185.90\nG. $192.80\nH. $199.50\nI. $165.30\nJ. $205.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
