      "generated_answer": "First, calculate the wall area: there are two walls of 14' × 8.5' and two of 10' × 8.5'. Total area = 2(14×8.5) + 2(10×8.5) = 238 + 170 = 408 sq ft. Each quart covers 36 sq ft, so 408 ÷ 36 ≈ 11.33 → round up to 12 quarts (since fraction requires full quart). Cost: 12 × ($9.80 + $5) = 12 × $14.80 = $177.60.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
