  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_706",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the refund on an insurance policy with anannual premiumof $37 that is canceled 33 days after it was purchased?\n\nOptions: \nA. $28.40\nB. $30.50\nC. $7.40\nD. $34.60\nE. $31.10\nF. $32.20\nG. $25.00\nH. $29.60\nI. $35.60\nJ. $33.70\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Assuming a 365-day year and a short-rate cancellation (no refund for partial periods), the insurer keeps the full premium for the time the policy was in force. The daily premium is $37 / 365 ≈ $0.1014, so for 33 days, the earned premium is 33 × $0.1014 ≈ $3.35. The refund would be $37 − $3.35 = $33.65, closest to $33.70.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
