      "generated_answer": "We use the put-call parity and currency option symmetry (reciprocal strike and exchange of currencies). The dollar-denominated put on yen corresponds to a yen-denominated call on dollars, and via symmetry, we transform the given put price using the spot rate and interest rates. Applying the transformation: $ P_{¥}(K=125) = (1/S_0) \\cdot e^{(r_{¥} - r_\\$)T} \\cdot [K^2 \\cdot P_{\\$}(K')] $ with appropriate adjustments, the calculated price is closest to 42.77325.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
