    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, calculate the cost of goods sold (COGS) using the 45% margin on sales: a 45% margin means the cost is 55% of sales, so COGS = 55% × $72,600 = $39,930. Then, compute the cost of goods available for sale: beginning inventory ($30,156) + purchases ($28,300) = $58,456. Subtract COGS from goods available: $58,456 − $39,930 = $18,526, which is the estimated ending inventory.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
