    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_440",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider a strategy of the form $(\\gamma, 0, 0)$ for the investment wheel. Show that the overall factor multiplying your money after $n$ steps is likely to be $(1+2\\gamma)^{{n/2}}(1-\\gamma)^{{n/2}}$. Find the value of $\\gamma$ that maximizes this factor.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.80\nB. 0.25\nC. 0.10\nD. 0.33\nE. 0.50\nF. 0.66\nG. 1.00\nH. 0.20\nI. 0.40\nJ. 0.75\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are maximizing the factor $(1+2\\gamma)^{n/2}(1-\\gamma)^{n/2}$. Taking the $n$th root, we maximize the per-step growth rate:  \n$f(\\gamma) = (1+2\\gamma)^{1/2}(1-\\gamma)^{1/2}$.  \nMaximizing $f(\\gamma)$ is equivalent to maximizing $\\ln f(\\gamma) = \\frac{1}{2}[\\ln(1+2\\gamma) + \\ln(1-\\gamma)]$. Taking derivative and setting to zero:  \n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{1+2\\gamma} - \\frac{1}{1-\\gamma}\\right) = 0 \\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{1+2\\gamma} = \\frac{1}{1-\\gamma} \\Rightarrow 2(1-\\gamma) = 1+2\\gamma \\Rightarrow 2 - 2\\gamma = 1 + 2\\gamma \\Rightarrow 1 = 4\\gamma \\Rightarrow \\gamma = 0.25.\n$$\n\nThus, the value of $\\gamma$ that maximizes the growth factor is $0.25$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 173,
        "output_tokens": 175,
        "total_tokens": 348
