    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_108",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has been found that hours of recreation (r) and wages (W) have a direct effect on productivity (P), so that : P =ar+bW. In two surveys it was found that Survey 1P = 170 : r = 51 : W = 136 Survey 2P = 425 : r = 68 : W = 204 What are the values of a and b ?\n\nOptions: \nA. a = 68, b = 204\nB. a = 2, b = 1.25\nC. a = 0, b = 3\nD. a = 170, b = 425\nE. a = 5, b = 2\nF. a = 4, b = 1.5\nG. a = 3, b = 0.5\nH. a = -20, b = 8.75\nI. a = 51, b = 136\nJ. a = 10, b = 0.85\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given the equation $ P = ar + bW $ and two data points:  \n- Survey 1: $ 170 = 51a + 136b $  \n- Survey 2: $ 425 = 68a + 204b $\n\nSolving this system: multiply the first equation by 3: $ 510 = 153a + 408b $, and the second by 2: $ 850 = 136a + 408b $. Subtract: $ 340 = 17a \\Rightarrow a = 20 $. Substituting back: $ 170 = 51(20) + 136b \\Rightarrow 170 = 1020 + 136b \\Rightarrow b = -6.25 $. But this doesn’t match any option.\n\nWait — recheck calculations. Try option B: $ a = 2, b = 1.25 $:  \nSurvey 1: $ 2(51) + 1.25(136) = 102 + 170 = 272 \\neq 170 $. Not good.\n\nTry option G: $ a = 3, b = 0.5 $:  \n1: $ 3(51) + 0.5(136) = 153 + 68 = 221 \\neq 170 $\n\nTry option F: $ a = 4, b = 1.5 $: $ 4(51) = 204, 1.5(136) = 204, sum = 408 $ — too big.\n\nTry option H: $ a = -20, b = 8.75 $:  \nSurvey 1: $ -20(51) + 8.75(136) = -1020 + 1190 = 170 $ ✅  \nSurvey 2: $ -20(68) + 8.75(204) = -1360 + 1785 = 425 $ ✅\n\nThis matches perfectly.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
      "success": true,
