    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_480",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compare the costs of a $5,000 20-year endowment policy with a $5,000 20-year limited payment policy if each were to be purchased at age 45.\n\nOptions: \nA. $182.45\nB. $125.75\nC. $233.35\nD. $300.20\nE. $160.65\nF. $99.99\nG. $46.67\nH. $210.10\nI. $75.50\nJ. $50.90\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The 20-year endowment policy requires premiums to be paid throughout the 20-year period, while the 20-year limited payment policy allows the premiums to be paid over a shorter duration but with higher annual costs. However, since both policies provide the same death benefit and endow at the end of 20 years, the total premium paid for the limited payment policy is generally higher annually but over fewer years. Given typical actuarial calculations, the endowment policy (with level payments over 20 years) usually has lower annual premiums, and based on standard rate tables, the most plausible annual cost comparison for the endowment policy at age 45 is around $182.45.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
