    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To forecast 10-day volatility using a GARCH model, the correct approach is to obtain the 10-step ahead forecast of the conditional variance, which represents the predicted variance at a specific future point, and then take its square root to get the standard deviation (volatility). This directly estimates the volatility for the 10th day ahead, which is appropriate for value at risk calculations requiring a point forecast of volatility.\n\nThe other options incorrectly combine multiple forecasts or scale them in ways not supported by GARCH dynamics or volatility aggregation principles.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
