    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6389",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that two researchers, using the same 3 variables and the same 250 observations on each variable, estimate a VAR. One estimates a VAR(6), while the other estimates a VAR(4). The determinants of the variance-covariance matrices of the residuals for each VAR are 0.0036 and 0.0049 respectively. What is the values of the test statistic for performing a test of whether the VAR(6) can be restricted to a VAR(4)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4.87\nB. 9.21\nC. 6.45\nD. 0.31\nE. 0.33\nF. 2.75\nG. 77.07\nH. 5.89\nI. 3.67\nJ. 1.27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The test statistic for comparing two VAR models (VAR(6) vs VAR(4)) using the determinant of the residual covariance matrix is based on the likelihood ratio test:  \n$ \\text{LR} = T \\left[ \\ln|\\hat{\\Sigma}_\\text{restricted}| - \\ln|\\hat{\\Sigma}_\\text{unrestricted}| \\right] $,  \nwhere $ T = 250 $, $ |\\hat{\\Sigma}_\\text{unrestricted}| = 0.0036 $ (VAR(6)), and $ |\\hat{\\Sigma}_\\text{restricted}| = 0.0049 $ (VAR(4)).  \n\nThen, $ \\text{LR} = 250 [\\ln(0.0049) - \\ln(0.0036)] = 250 \\ln(0.0049/0.0036) = 250 \\ln(1.3611) \\approx 250 \\times 0.308 \\approx 77.07 $.  \n\nThus, the correct answer is $ \\boxed{G} $.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 252,
        "output_tokens": 250,
