      "generated_answer": "The question states that the benefits of education extend beyond Chris to society as a whole, such as making him a better voter, parent, and citizen. This indicates the presence of positive externalities. When an activity generates positive externalities, it is often underprovided in a free market, so economists typically recommend subsidization to encourage more of it.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
