      "generated_answer": "For an MA(1) process with zero mean, $ X_t = \\epsilon_t + \\theta \\epsilon_{t-1} $, the autocovariance at lag 1 is given by $ \\gamma(1) = \\theta \\sigma^2 $, where $ \\sigma^2 $ is the variance of the white noise error term $ \\epsilon_t $. Since the moving average coefficient $ \\theta = 0.4 $, but $ \\sigma^2 $ is not provided, we cannot compute the exact value of the autocovariance without it.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{J}.",
