    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a competitive firm, what is the most important thing to consider in deciding whether to shut down in the short run?\n\nOptions: \nA. Do not produce if the TFC is not covered by revenue.\nB. Do not produce if the price is lower than AVC.\nC. Compare AVC to MR.\nD. Compare AFC to MR.\nE. Shut down if the firm is not making a profit.\nF. Do not produce if the TVC is not covered by revenue.\nG. Compare the price of inputs to the price of the product.\nH. Compare TR to TC.\nI. Produce the highest quantity demanded regardless of price.\nJ. Produce as long as the price is higher than AVC.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
