      "generated_answer": "In a lien theory state, a mortgage serves as a lien on the property but does not transfer title. The majority view holds that a mortgage by one joint tenant does not sever the joint tenancy or destroy the right of survivorship. Therefore, when the mortgagor dies, the surviving joint tenant acquires full title by operation of law, and the mortgage lien is extinguished.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
