      "generated_answer": "The federal government, under the Commerce Clause, has broad authority to regulate interstate commerce, which includes the extraction and distribution of critical natural resources like pitchblende. When Congress enacts a valid federal law that conflicts with state law, the Supremacy Clause of the U.S. Constitution renders the conflicting state law invalid. Since the federal statute explicitly forbids states from taxing pitchblende extraction, the state tax is preempted and therefore invalid.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
