    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1804",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Congress enacts a statute that makes Pennsylvania Avenue a one-way street. Congress has enacted the statute solely for the purpose of enabling members of Congress to travel back and forth to the Capital without being tied up in heavy traffic each day. Before Congress enacted this law, the Washington, D. C. , City Council had previously passed an ordinance designating Pennsylvania Avenue as a two-lane street. Which of the following is the most accurate statement regarding the constitutionality of the federal statute designating Pennsylvania Avenue a one-way street?\n\nOptions: \nA. It is invalid because it conflicts with the ordinance passed by the Washington, D.C., City Council.\nB. It is valid as it is within the purview of Congress's power over transportation.\nC. It is invalid because the law infringes upon the rights of the residents of Washington, D.C.\nD. It is invalid because it is a discriminatory burden on interstate commerce.\nE. It is valid because it is a proper exercise of Congress's enumerated property power.\nF. It is invalid because it violates the Tenth Amendment.\nG. It is valid because Congress has exclusive power over the District of Columbia.\nH. It is valid because Congress has the power to regulate interstate commerce.\nI. It is invalid because the Washington, D. C. , City Council has exclusive power over the public thoroughfares within the District of Columbia.\nJ. It is valid because it serves a clear governmental interest.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most accurate statement is that Congress has exclusive authority over the District of Columbia under Article I, Section 8, Clause 17 of the U.S. Constitution, which allows it to exercise full legislative power, including over local matters like traffic regulations. While the D.C. City Council can pass laws under home rule, Congress retains ultimate authority and can override local ordinances. Therefore, the federal statute designating Pennsylvania Avenue as one-way is valid due to Congress's exclusive legislative power over the District.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
