    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The country club’s interest is best described as a fee simple subject to an executory limitation because the deed grants an estate that can automatically terminate upon a specified event (use contrary to the restrictions), with future enjoyment shifting to another use or reverting to the grantor or its successors. The clause allowing the grantor to \"re-enter and terminate the estate\" upon breach indicates an executory interest in the grantor, which is characteristic of an executory limitation. This structure does not create a determinable fee with a possibility of reverter, but rather a fee simple subject to an executory interest.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
