      "generated_answer": "The original deed restriction requiring minimum two-acre lots for single-family dwellings only was expressly binding on all subsequent grantees and was included in the deeds for phase 1, making it enforceable against those lot owners. Although the surrounding area was rezoned commercially and phase 2 ignored the restriction, this does not automatically terminate enforceability in phase 1, especially since the restriction was properly recorded and applied there. Therefore, the court will most likely hold that the restrictions are still enforceable against phase 1 homeowners.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
