      "generated_answer": "The ordinance mandates that all waste within the city limits—regardless of origin—must be processed at a local facility, which appears neutral on its face. However, in cases like *United Haulers Ass’n v. Oneida-Herkimer Solid Waste Management Authority*, the Supreme Court upheld similar flow control laws if they serve a legitimate local purpose like health and safety and do not clearly favor in-state interests. Here, the ordinance applies equally to all waste within the city, so it is not facially discriminatory.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
