      "generated_answer": "Let $ D $, $ G $, $ S $, and $ H $ denote the sets of residents who own a diamond ring, golf clubs, a garden spade, and candy hearts, respectively. Since all 900 residents own candy hearts, $ H $ includes everyone, so owning \"all four\" things is equivalent to owning a diamond ring, golf clubs, and a garden spade (in addition to the universal candy hearts).\n\nWe are given:\n- $ |D| = 195 $\n- $ |G| = 367 $\n- $ |S| = 562 $\n- All 900 own $ H $\n- 437 own **exactly two** of the four items\n- 234 own **exactly three** of the four items\nLet $ x $ be the number who own **all four** items.\n\nSince everyone owns candy hearts, the ownership of the other three items determines the count:\n- A person who owns a collection of items including $ H $ and exactly $ k $ of $ D, G, S $ owns $ k+1 $ items in total.\n\nSo:\n- Owning exactly two of the four items → owns $ H $ and exactly one of $ D, G, S $\n- Owning exactly three of the four items → owns $ H $ and exactly two of $ D, G, S $\n- Owning all four → owns $ H $ and all three of $ D, G, S $\n\nLet:\n- $ A $: number who own exactly 1 of $ D, G, S $ → these are the 437\n- $ B $: number who own exactly 2 of $ D, G, S $ → these are the 234\n- $ x $: number who own all 3 of $ D, G, S $\n\nThen the total number of residents is:\n$$\n\\text{(owns 1 of D,G,S)} + \\text{(owns 2)} + \\text{(owns 3)} + \\text{(owns none)} = 900\n$$\nSo:\n$$\n437 + 234 + x + N = 900 \\Rightarrow N = 900 - (437 + 234 + x) = 229 - x\n$$\nwhere $ N $ is the number who own **none** of $ D, G, S $.\n\nNow use the principle of inclusion-exclusion for the total count of people who own at least one of $ D, G, S $:\n$$\n|D \\cup G \\cup S| = |D| + |G| + |S| - |D \\cap G| - |D \\cap S| - |G \\cap S| + |D \\cap G \\cap S|\n$$\nBut $ |D \\cup G \\cup S| = 900 - N = 900 - (229 - x) = 671 + x $\n\nOn the other hand, we can compute the sum of sizes using counts by number of items owned.\n\nLet’s compute the total number of times these items are owned:\n- Each person who owns exactly 1 of $ D,G,S $ contributes 1 to the sum $ |D| + |G| + |S| $\n- Each who owns exactly 2 contributes 2\n- Each who owns 3 contributes 3\n- Each who owns 0 contributes 0\n\nSo total sum:\n$$\n|D| + |G| + |S| = 195 + 367 + 562 = 1124\n$$\nAnd also:\n$$\n= (1)(437) + (2)(234) + (3)(x) + (0)(N) = 437 + 468 + 3x = 905 + 0x + 3x? Wait:\n$$\n$ 437 \\times 1 = 437 $  \n$ 234 \\times 2 = 468 $  \n$ x \\times 3 = 3x $  \nSo total:\n$$\n437 + 468 + 3x = 905 + 3x\n$$\nSet equal to 1124:\n$$\n905 + 3x = 1124 \\Rightarrow 3x = 219 \\Rightarrow x = 73\n$$\n\nThus, the number of residents who own all four items is $ \\boxed{73} $.",
