      "generated_answer": "We analyze the functions $ f(x) = \\left| |x| - \\frac{1}{2} \\right| $ and $ g(x) = \\left| |x| - \\frac{1}{4} \\right| $, both of which are even and periodic in behavior due to the absolute values. The compositions $ y = 4g(f(\\sin(2\\pi x))) $ and $ x = 4g(f(\\cos(3\\pi y))) $ are highly oscillatory but bounded and piecewise constant due to the periodic nature of sine and cosine and the nested absolute values, leading to a finite number of intersections. By analyzing the periods and ranges, and noting symmetry and functional behavior, the graphs intersect exactly **16** times.\n\n\\boxed{16}",
