ifferences from each pair), and for |S|=3 in Z8, |S-S| ≤ 7 for all S? Can |S-S| = 8? That would be the whole group.\n\nFor example, S={0,1,3} as above has |S-S|=7.\n\nS={0,1,2}: differences: 0,1,2,7,6,0, etc: 0-0=0,0-1=7,0-2=6,1-0=1,1-1=0,1-2=7,2-0=2,2-1=1,2-2=0, so values: 0,1,2,6,7. So {0,1,2,6,7} size 5 <8.\n\nS={0,1,4}: diff:0-1=7,0-4=4,1-0=1,1-4=5,4-0=4,4-1=3,4-4=0, etc: 0,7,4,1,5,3,4,3,0,... so values: 0,1,3,4,5,7. Size 6.\n\nS={0,2,3}: diff:0-2=6,0-3=5,2-0=2,2-3=7,3-0=3,3-2=1, so 0,6,5,2,7,3,1 — that's 8 elements? 0,1,2,3,5,6,7, and 4? Is 4 in? 0- something=4? 0-4 not in S, 2-6 not, 3-7 not, so no. S-S = {0,1,2,3,5,6,7} size 7.\n\nCan we get 8? Suppose S={0,1,3}, got 7.\n\nS={0,1,5}: diff:0-1=7,0-5=3,1-0=1,1-5=4,5-0=5,5-1=4,5-5=0,1-0=1,0-0=0, etc. Values: 0,7,3,1,4,5. So {0,1,3,4,5,7} size 6.\n\nMaximum is 7 for |S|=3 in Z8.\n\nSimilarly, minimum is 3, for example S={0,1,2}: differences include only up to 2 and down to 6,7, but in this case size 5.\n\nS={0,2,4}: differences: 0-2=6,0-4=4,2-0=2,2-4=6,4-0=4,4-2=2, so 0,2,4,6. Size 4.\n\nIs there S with |S-S|=3? Only if the differences are few, but with 3 elements, at least the pairwise differences, so at least 3 non-zero, plus 0, at least 4. So |S-S| ≥ 4 for |S|=3.\n\nFor example, S={0,1,7}: then differences: 0-1=7,0-7=1,1-0=1,1-7=2,7-0=7,7-1=6,7-7=0,1-0=1, etc. Values: 0,1,2,6,7. Size 5.\n\nSo min |S-S| = 4 (e.g. S={0,1,2} has 5, S={0,4,2} same), S={0,1,6}: 0-1=7,0-6=2,1-0=1,1-6=3,6-0=6,6-1=5, so {0,1,2,3,5,6,7} size 7.\n\nSeems minimum is 4? Let's find one. Suppose S={0,2,3}: earlier for {0,2,3}: differences from 0: 0,6 ( to 2), 5 ( to 3); from 2: 0,2 ( to 0), 7 ( to 3); from 3:0,3 ( to 0),1 ( to 2). So values: 0,1,2,3,5,6,7 — size 7.\n\nS={0,3,6}: then 0-3=5,0-6=2,3-0=3,3-6=5,6-0=6,6-3=3, so values: 0,2,3,5,6. Size 5.\n\nS={0,4,1}: as above, size 6.\n\nPerhaps all have |S-S| >= 5, but anyway, from above, |S-S| <= 7, so 8 - |S-S| >= 1 for all |S|=3.\n\nSo for every 3-element subset, there is at least one k suc