    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the original speed be $ s $ km/hr and the distance be $ d $ km. From the given conditions, the time taken originally is $ \\frac{d}{s} $. If he walks $ \\frac{1}{2} $ km/hr faster, he takes 1 hour less:  \n$$\n\\frac{d}{s + 0.5} = \\frac{d}{s} - 1\n$$\nIf he walks 1 km/hr slower, he takes 3 hours more:\n$$\n\\frac{d}{s - 1} = \\frac{d}{s} + 3\n$$\n\nSolving these equations simultaneously (by eliminating $ d $), we find $ s = 4 $ km/hr and $ d = 36 $ km.  \nThus, the distance is $ \\boxed{36} $ km and the original speed is $ \\boxed{4} $ km/hr.",
