    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The area of a trapezium is given by the formula:  \n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (a + b) \\times h\n$$\nwhere $ a $ and $ b $ are the lengths of the parallel sides (bases), and $ h $ is the height.  \nGiven the area is 84 cm², height is 8 cm, and the ratio of the bases is $ 2:5 $, let the bases be $ 2x $ and $ 5x $. Substituting into the formula:\n$$\n84 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (2x + 5x) \\times 8 = 4 \\times 7x = 28x\n\\Rightarrow x = 3\n$$\nSo the bases are $ 2x = 6 $ cm and $ 5x = 15 $ cm.  \n\\boxed{{6\\,\\text{cm}\\,\\text{and}\\,15\\,\\text{cm}}}",
