    "global index": "AsDiv_1412",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Ten years ago, the sum of the ages of two sons was one-third of their father's age. One son is two years older than the other and sum of their present ages is 14 years less than the father's present age.\n\nQuestion: Find the present ages of all.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the present ages of the younger son be $ x $ and the older son be $ x + 2 $. Ten years ago, their ages were $ x - 10 $ and $ x + 2 - 10 = x - 8 $, and the sum was $ (x - 10) + (x - 8) = 2x - 18 $. This sum was one-third of the father's age at that time, so if the father's present age is $ f $, then ten years ago it was $ f - 10 $, giving:  \n$$\n2x - 18 = \\frac{1}{3}(f - 10)\n\\Rightarrow 6x - 54 = f - 10\n\\Rightarrow f = 6x - 44.\n$$  \nAlso, the sum of the sons' present ages is 14 less than the father's:  \n$$\nx + (x + 2) = f - 14\n\\Rightarrow 2x + 2 = f - 14.\n$$  \nSubstitute $ f = 6x - 44 $:  \n$$\n2x + 2 = 6x - 44 - 14\n\\Rightarrow 2x + 2 = 6x - 58\n\\Rightarrow 60 = 4x\n\\Rightarrow x = 15.\n$$  \nThus, the younger son is 15, the older is 17, and the father is $ f = 6(15) - 44 = 90 - 44 = 46 $.  \n\nFinal answer:  \n\\boxed{{15, 17, 46}}",
